WEBVTT

1
00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.350
- <i>Seq, I'm in.</i>
- <i>Captain.</i>

2
00:00:59.433 --> 00:01:00.685
<i>You were right.</i>

3
00:01:00.768 --> 00:01:02.186
<i>The skylight
was a window pane.</i>

4
00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:03.771
<i>I've got
serious interference.</i>

5
00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:05.189
<i>Weird.
It's some kind of Modal.</i>

6
00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:07.066
<i>Looks like old code.</i>

7
00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.526
<i>It feels
really familiar.</i>

8
00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:10.361
<i>Drop a pin.
I'll signal for backup.</i>

9
00:01:10.444 --> 00:01:12.113
- <i>I'm gonna check it out.</i>
- <i>Bugs?</i>

10
00:01:12.196 --> 00:01:13.406
<i>If the general finds out
we've been fishing...</i>

11
00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:15.158
<i>A quick peek can't hurt.</i>

12
00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.534
<i>Did you hear that?</i>

13
00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:17.994
<i>Shit. I think
our signal was traced.</i>

14
00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.204
<i>Bugs, this feels like a trap.</i>

15
00:01:20.288 --> 00:01:21.414
<i>Bugs!</i>

16
00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.873
Freeze!
Do not move!

17
00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:04.916
We will shoot!

18
00:02:04.999 --> 00:02:08.294
Very slowly, raise your hands.

19
00:02:22.183 --> 00:02:23.768
Here we go.

20
00:02:29.607 --> 00:02:31.108
Hey, where are you going?

21
00:02:31.192 --> 00:02:32.401
You were warned, Lieutenant.

22
00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.737
I think we can handle
one little girl.

23
00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.283
You're wasting your time!

24
00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:41.619
My men are bringing her
down now.

25
00:02:41.702 --> 00:02:42.787
No, Lieutenant,

26
00:02:43.871 --> 00:02:45.873
your men are already dead.

27
00:02:56.425 --> 00:02:57.677
Seq, you with me?

28
00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.136
This old code keeps crashing.

29
00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.554
Your projection's breaking up.
Switch to audio.

30
00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:01.973
Bugs,
this is a direct violation

31
00:03:02.056 --> 00:03:03.307
of the general's protocols.

32
00:03:03.391 --> 00:03:04.809
I know, I know.

33
00:03:04.892 --> 00:03:06.519
But something
is happening here.

34
00:03:07.395 --> 00:03:09.146
Something important.

35
00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.314
Oh, fuck.

36
00:03:10.398 --> 00:03:11.983
We know what happens next.

37
00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:13.734
She kicks their ass.

38
00:03:36.257 --> 00:03:37.675
Now she makes a call.

39
00:03:37.758 --> 00:03:39.010
The line was traced.

40
00:03:39.093 --> 00:03:41.345
- And then...
- Then she runs for her life.

41
00:03:41.429 --> 00:03:42.763
Are there any agents?

42
00:03:42.847 --> 00:03:44.265
We know this story.

43
00:03:45.808 --> 00:03:47.435
This is how it all began.

44
00:03:48.144 --> 00:03:49.979
God damn it.

45
00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:51.522
This is where he began.

46
00:03:51.605 --> 00:03:54.859
You're thinking this Modal
is a loop? Or a treadmill?

47
00:03:54.942 --> 00:03:58.487
Some sort of sequencer
evolving a program to do what?

48
00:03:58.571 --> 00:03:59.739
I don't know.

49
00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:02.533
But I'm going to find out.

50
00:04:02.616 --> 00:04:03.743
All right.

51
00:04:34.357 --> 00:04:36.734
So deja vu and yet it's
obviously all wrong.

52
00:04:36.817 --> 00:04:38.986
Why use old code
to mirror something new?

53
00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.696
I don't know.

54
00:04:54.085 --> 00:04:55.419
If that's supposed
to be Trinity,

55
00:04:55.503 --> 00:04:57.046
that's not what happens.

56
00:04:59.006 --> 00:05:00.966
Maybe this isn't the story
we think it is.

57
00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.427
Bugs, you have
to get out of here.

58
00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:05.763
It's gotta be a trap.

59
00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:08.224
Shit.

60
00:05:45.928 --> 00:05:47.263
Uh...

61
00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:49.140
You all carry on.

62
00:05:49.223 --> 00:05:50.224
As you were.

63
00:05:53.227 --> 00:05:54.770
I'm just gonna...

64
00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.440
see myself out.

65
00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.524
Kill her.

66
00:06:32.683 --> 00:06:34.477
Oh, Seq!

67
00:07:42.169 --> 00:07:43.587
- Why did you save me?
- You first.

68
00:07:43.671 --> 00:07:45.422
Who are you?
Where did you come from?

69
00:07:45.506 --> 00:07:47.049
Okay.

70
00:07:47.132 --> 00:07:48.884
My name is Bugs.

71
00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:51.262
As in "Bunny."

72
00:07:51.345 --> 00:07:53.055
And tech that listens.

73
00:07:54.139 --> 00:07:56.100
Do you know this is a Modal?

74
00:07:57.351 --> 00:07:58.477
What's a Modal?

75
00:07:58.561 --> 00:08:00.854
It's a simulation
used to evolve programs.

76
00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.610
Do you understand
that you are...

77
00:08:07.528 --> 00:08:09.196
digital sentience?

78
00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:10.948
I know what I am.

79
00:08:11.031 --> 00:08:12.283
Just like I know my job

80
00:08:12.366 --> 00:08:14.451
is to hunt down
and destroy synthients.

81
00:08:14.535 --> 00:08:15.786
Like you.

82
00:08:19.957 --> 00:08:21.500
And yet...

83
00:08:23.252 --> 00:08:24.587
Here we are.

84
00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.088
Here we are.

85
00:08:27.548 --> 00:08:29.842
The other agents
don't know about this room?

86
00:08:31.802 --> 00:08:32.970
How'd you find it?

87
00:08:33.053 --> 00:08:35.556
No one was ever
in the key shop,

88
00:08:35.639 --> 00:08:36.849
so I started looking.

89
00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:40.102
More you looked,
the more you found.

90
00:08:41.145 --> 00:08:42.730
Story of my life.

91
00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:50.863
What?

92
00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:54.617
I feel like I know this room.

93
00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.669
Holy shit.

94
00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:09.506
This is his apartment.

95
00:09:10.758 --> 00:09:12.843
You mean Thomas Anderson's?

96
00:09:12.926 --> 00:09:14.887
I searched everywhere.
He doesn't exist.

97
00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:17.222
He stopped being Thomas
a long time ago,

98
00:09:17.306 --> 00:09:19.683
but maybe you know him
by his real name.

99
00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:21.518
Neo.

100
00:09:22.978 --> 00:09:24.229
You do.

101
00:09:25.314 --> 00:09:26.899
Oh, okay.

102
00:09:27.566 --> 00:09:28.859
Uh...

103
00:09:28.942 --> 00:09:31.570
I can't believe this,
after all these years.

104
00:09:31.654 --> 00:09:35.324
You see, most people
think that Neo is dead.

105
00:09:36.659 --> 00:09:38.077
But I know he's not.

106
00:09:39.036 --> 00:09:40.788
Because I've seen him.

107
00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.833
Where?

108
00:09:44.917 --> 00:09:47.461
It's not something
I can explain easily, but...

109
00:09:51.966 --> 00:09:55.094
<i>But the moment
he looked at me,</i>

110
00:09:55.177 --> 00:09:56.804
I felt something...

111
00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:01.850
unlock my mind.

112
00:10:04.395 --> 00:10:05.479
Okay.

113
00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:09.733
Something like that
happened to me.

114
00:10:14.655 --> 00:10:16.323
<i>I saw this pattern...</i>

115
00:10:17.616 --> 00:10:19.034
<i>and it was everywhere.</i>

116
00:10:20.661 --> 00:10:23.038
We can't see it,
but we're all trapped inside

117
00:10:23.122 --> 00:10:25.666
these strange,
repeating loops.

118
00:10:25.749 --> 00:10:29.002
Somehow I saw it
in the mirror.

119
00:10:29.086 --> 00:10:31.839
Just a flicker,
but it was like you said.

120
00:10:37.344 --> 00:10:39.722
And suddenly I understood.

121
00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:42.266
This is not the real world.

122
00:10:44.727 --> 00:10:48.063
<i>For the first time,
I felt real purpose.</i>

123
00:10:48.731 --> 00:10:50.691
I knew who I was

124
00:10:50.774 --> 00:10:52.693
and what I had to do.

125
00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:54.778
Who are you?

126
00:10:56.113 --> 00:10:57.823
What do you have to do?

127
00:11:00.784 --> 00:11:02.077
I am...

128
00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.246
Morpheus.

129
00:11:05.372 --> 00:11:07.666
And I have to find Neo.

130
00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:13.172
Morpheus.

131
00:11:16.133 --> 00:11:17.760
Okay. Okay.

132
00:11:17.843 --> 00:11:18.927
Oh, my God!

133
00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:20.304
I have to get you out of here.

134
00:11:20.387 --> 00:11:22.806
I need to figure out
who built this Modal.

135
00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:24.475
Okay, come with me.

136
00:11:24.558 --> 00:11:26.685
You have to be ready to leave.
You have to be really ready.

137
00:11:26.769 --> 00:11:28.061
And if you're not,

138
00:11:28.145 --> 00:11:29.146
if you think that
this is where you belong...

139
00:11:32.649 --> 00:11:34.067
You call this a choice?

140
00:11:34.151 --> 00:11:35.652
Oh, honestly, when somebody
offered me these things,

141
00:11:35.736 --> 00:11:37.237
I went off on binary
conceptions of the world

142
00:11:37.321 --> 00:11:38.906
and said there was no way
I was swallowing

143
00:11:38.989 --> 00:11:40.866
some symbolic reduction
of my life.

144
00:11:40.949 --> 00:11:42.284
And the woman
with the pills laughed

145
00:11:42.367 --> 00:11:43.535
'cause I was
missing the point.

146
00:11:43.619 --> 00:11:45.162
What point?

147
00:11:45.245 --> 00:11:48.165
The choice is an illusion.

148
00:11:48.248 --> 00:11:50.459
You already know
what you have to do.

149
00:11:57.216 --> 00:11:58.300
Truth.

150
00:12:05.015 --> 00:12:06.016
Okay.

151
00:12:06.099 --> 00:12:07.309
There's an old building

152
00:12:07.392 --> 00:12:08.977
with a skylight
and lots of stairs.

153
00:12:09.061 --> 00:12:10.270
The Lafayette.

154
00:12:10.354 --> 00:12:11.897
One of the four back doors
leads there.

155
00:12:12.731 --> 00:12:13.857
Oh.

156
00:12:13.941 --> 00:12:15.442
- Don't fight it.
- Whoa, what's happening?

157
00:12:15.526 --> 00:12:16.610
Keep breathing.

158
00:12:16.693 --> 00:12:18.070
Extraction works
pretty much the same

159
00:12:18.153 --> 00:12:20.072
for humans and programs.

160
00:12:22.908 --> 00:12:23.909
Ouch.

161
00:12:23.992 --> 00:12:25.035
Ah.

162
00:12:26.453 --> 00:12:27.746
Okay.

163
00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:31.708
- Hey.
- Hey.

164
00:12:31.792 --> 00:12:33.585
I've never worn
different glasses before.

165
00:12:33.669 --> 00:12:36.421
Yeah, looks good.
Which door?

166
00:12:36.505 --> 00:12:38.298
- It's gotta be...
- Okay.

167
00:12:43.345 --> 00:12:45.055
Agent White.

168
00:12:45.138 --> 00:12:46.348
Agent Smith?

169
00:12:52.062 --> 00:12:53.522
Go!

170
00:13:00.737 --> 00:13:02.406
Seq! Can you hear me?

171
00:13:02.489 --> 00:13:03.740
Bugs! I thought I lost you.

172
00:13:03.824 --> 00:13:05.075
Can you get us
to the window pane?

173
00:13:05.158 --> 00:13:07.119
Bugs! Bugs! He's an agent!

174
00:13:17.296 --> 00:13:19.548
That window! Go hard!

175
00:14:05.761 --> 00:14:08.221
What the...

176
00:14:14.519 --> 00:14:16.480
What the hell?

177
00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:34.665
Something wrong?

178
00:14:34.748 --> 00:14:37.501
Uh... Just a little crash.

179
00:14:37.584 --> 00:14:39.962
Morning, Bobbi. Morning, dude.

180
00:14:40.045 --> 00:14:43.840
What a beautiful day
to be alive. Am I right?

181
00:14:43.924 --> 00:14:45.926
- Problemo?
- He lost something.

182
00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:48.553
Is this old <i>Matrix</i> code?

183
00:14:50.555 --> 00:14:52.140
A little Modal experiment.

184
00:14:52.224 --> 00:14:55.185
For <i>Binary?</i>

185
00:14:55.268 --> 00:14:57.896
- I need a coffee.
- Coffee. Yes, stat!

186
00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.106
I'm buying.

187
00:15:02.109 --> 00:15:03.860
I'm not trying to blow
smoke up your ass,

188
00:15:03.944 --> 00:15:08.365
but the first time I played
the trilogy, I was shook.

189
00:15:08.448 --> 00:15:11.034
The paradox
between free will and destiny.

190
00:15:11.118 --> 00:15:12.285
Are we all just algorithms

191
00:15:12.369 --> 00:15:13.578
doing what we're
supposed to do

192
00:15:13.662 --> 00:15:15.372
or can we escape
our programming?

193
00:15:15.455 --> 00:15:19.376
Genius, inside the context
of the game, BT dubs.

194
00:15:19.459 --> 00:15:21.545
Hey, did I tell you
it took over my life?

195
00:15:21.628 --> 00:15:24.381
Yeah. I failed
the seventh grade.

196
00:15:24.464 --> 00:15:26.633
Your game almost ruined me.

197
00:15:26.717 --> 00:15:29.219
- So you've said.
- Yet here we are.

198
00:15:29.302 --> 00:15:32.139
You tell me, Mr. Anderson,

199
00:15:32.222 --> 00:15:33.265
is it free will

200
00:15:34.516 --> 00:15:36.143
or destiny?

201
00:15:40.814 --> 00:15:42.733
Oh, yeah.

202
00:15:42.816 --> 00:15:44.735
There she is.

203
00:15:44.818 --> 00:15:46.319
Total f-ing MILF.

204
00:15:47.195 --> 00:15:49.281
Daggers. Look, I'm sorry.

205
00:15:49.364 --> 00:15:51.658
I'm a geek.
I was raised by machines.

206
00:15:51.742 --> 00:15:52.993
Maybe you should go.

207
00:15:53.076 --> 00:15:56.121
No, please.
I... I promise, best self.

208
00:15:56.204 --> 00:15:57.456
Best self.

209
00:16:01.376 --> 00:16:02.627
Sure.

210
00:16:03.503 --> 00:16:04.921
You ever talk to her?

211
00:16:07.049 --> 00:16:08.467
Tell you what.

212
00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:12.929
For all you've done for me,
let me do this for you.

213
00:16:13.013 --> 00:16:15.766
Jude, no. Stop.

214
00:16:15.849 --> 00:16:17.559
- Excuse me. Excuse me.
- Thanks.

215
00:16:17.642 --> 00:16:19.061
Hi. Um...

216
00:16:19.144 --> 00:16:20.729
I know this is all
a bit extemporaneous.

217
00:16:20.812 --> 00:16:22.439
I'm Jude Gallagher.

218
00:16:22.522 --> 00:16:25.108
I work for a game company
called Deus Machina.

219
00:16:25.192 --> 00:16:26.443
Hi, Jude, I'm Tiffany.

220
00:16:26.526 --> 00:16:29.446
Tiffany. Wow.
Didn't see that coming.

221
00:16:29.529 --> 00:16:31.448
- Mom loved Audrey Hepburn.
- Jude.

222
00:16:31.531 --> 00:16:35.452
Oh, and this is my very
good friend, Thomas Anderson.

223
00:16:35.535 --> 00:16:37.454
He is a bona fide
famous person

224
00:16:37.537 --> 00:16:38.914
and considered by most to be

225
00:16:38.997 --> 00:16:40.999
the greatest game designer
of our generation.

226
00:16:41.083 --> 00:16:42.292
I'm sorry about this.

227
00:16:42.375 --> 00:16:43.585
- Jude...
- Just talk to her.

228
00:16:43.668 --> 00:16:46.171
Hi, Thomas.
Everyone calls me "Tiff."

229
00:16:47.047 --> 00:16:48.256
Hi.

230
00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:56.556
Have we met?

231
00:16:58.016 --> 00:17:00.143
Uh, we both come here.

232
00:17:00.227 --> 00:17:01.645
- Can I have your morning bun?
- Hey!

233
00:17:01.728 --> 00:17:03.146
Are you trying
to ball my mom or what?

234
00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:04.523
Brandon!

235
00:17:04.606 --> 00:17:06.483
Can I have one bite?

236
00:17:06.566 --> 00:17:09.569
Babe! What's going on?
We're gonna be late.

237
00:17:09.653 --> 00:17:11.571
This is my husband, Chad.

238
00:17:11.655 --> 00:17:13.448
- Nice to meet you.
- Hey.

239
00:17:15.075 --> 00:17:17.160
Babe, we gotta get
Callie to practice.

240
00:17:17.244 --> 00:17:19.329
Right. Sorry.

241
00:17:19.413 --> 00:17:21.039
Come on, kids. Let's move out.

242
00:17:45.397 --> 00:17:46.398
What?

243
00:17:53.864 --> 00:17:56.199
Sorry. Uh, it's the boss.

244
00:18:02.122 --> 00:18:05.208
"Billions of people
just living out their lives...

245
00:18:06.418 --> 00:18:08.253
oblivious."

246
00:18:10.213 --> 00:18:12.591
I always loved that line.

247
00:18:12.674 --> 00:18:14.134
You wrote that one, yeah?

248
00:18:16.845 --> 00:18:19.014
Every time I stand here,

249
00:18:19.097 --> 00:18:22.350
I mean, O-M-G.

250
00:18:22.434 --> 00:18:24.477
It's so perfect,
it's gotta be fake.

251
00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:26.938
Right?

252
00:18:28.815 --> 00:18:30.066
Yeah.

253
00:18:30.817 --> 00:18:32.068
Sure.

254
00:18:32.152 --> 00:18:33.987
Have a seat.

255
00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:38.200
Smoke?

256
00:18:39.492 --> 00:18:40.535
I thought you quit.

257
00:18:41.411 --> 00:18:43.788
I quit calling it a habit.

258
00:18:43.872 --> 00:18:45.790
Now it's just
a guilty pleasure.

259
00:18:47.959 --> 00:18:51.546
Oh. Maybe I can make this
easy for you.

260
00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:53.673
I know <i>Binary</i> is over budget.

261
00:18:53.757 --> 00:18:56.051
This is not about <i>Binary,</i> Tom.
It's bigger than that.

262
00:18:56.134 --> 00:18:57.469
This is about our future,

263
00:18:57.552 --> 00:19:00.513
which is a sticky subject,
given our past.

264
00:19:00.597 --> 00:19:01.806
What do you mean?

265
00:19:02.933 --> 00:19:04.518
How's the therapy?

266
00:19:04.601 --> 00:19:05.894
Good.

267
00:19:06.603 --> 00:19:08.063
Any...

268
00:19:09.022 --> 00:19:10.357
episodes?

269
00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:13.235
No.

270
00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.654
That's terrific.

271
00:19:17.364 --> 00:19:20.867
Look, Tom, I know we've
always had our differences.

272
00:19:20.951 --> 00:19:22.786
What did you say
about our first meeting?

273
00:19:22.869 --> 00:19:26.122
We had all the chemistry
of an FBI interrogation.

274
00:19:28.833 --> 00:19:30.252
But look at this place.

275
00:19:31.336 --> 00:19:32.671
We did this.

276
00:19:34.047 --> 00:19:35.257
Together.

277
00:19:36.633 --> 00:19:38.093
Yeah.

278
00:19:38.176 --> 00:19:40.136
Now what?

279
00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:43.807
Things have changed.
The market's tough.

280
00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:46.184
I'm sure you can understand
why our beloved

281
00:19:46.268 --> 00:19:47.644
parent company, Warner Bros.,

282
00:19:47.727 --> 00:19:50.146
has decided to make
a sequel to the trilogy.

283
00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:51.648
What?

284
00:19:51.731 --> 00:19:53.650
They informed me they're gonna
do it with or without us.

285
00:19:53.733 --> 00:19:55.568
I thought
they couldn't do that.

286
00:19:56.778 --> 00:19:58.154
Oh, they can.

287
00:19:58.238 --> 00:19:59.572
And they made it clear

288
00:19:59.656 --> 00:20:01.825
they'll kill our contract
if we don't cooperate.

289
00:20:01.908 --> 00:20:03.618
Really?

290
00:20:03.702 --> 00:20:07.580
I know you said the story
was over for you,

291
00:20:07.664 --> 00:20:09.833
but that's the thing
about stories.

292
00:20:11.626 --> 00:20:13.545
They never really end,
do they?

293
00:20:13.628 --> 00:20:16.172
We're still telling the same
stories we've always told,

294
00:20:16.256 --> 00:20:20.552
just with different names,
different faces

295
00:20:22.178 --> 00:20:25.265
and I have to say
I'm kind of excited.

296
00:20:28.101 --> 00:20:29.269
After all these years,

297
00:20:29.352 --> 00:20:32.355
to be going back
to where it all started.

298
00:20:32.439 --> 00:20:34.774
Back to <i>The Matrix.</i>

299
00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:37.610
I've spoken to Marketing...

300
00:20:43.575 --> 00:20:45.118
Tom?

301
00:20:45.201 --> 00:20:46.745
Yeah.

302
00:20:46.828 --> 00:20:47.871
Are you all right?

303
00:20:50.206 --> 00:20:51.333
Yeah.

304
00:20:56.254 --> 00:20:58.465
What were you feeling
at that point?

305
00:21:01.551 --> 00:21:03.345
What was I feeling?

306
00:21:06.639 --> 00:21:11.394
I felt either I'm having
a mental breakdown again

307
00:21:11.478 --> 00:21:15.732
or I'm living inside
a computer-generated reality

308
00:21:15.815 --> 00:21:17.359
that has imprisoned me...

309
00:21:17.984 --> 00:21:19.152
again.

310
00:21:29.829 --> 00:21:31.331
Not much of a choice.

311
00:21:31.414 --> 00:21:32.624
No.

312
00:21:32.707 --> 00:21:34.292
Maybe it's not
as binary as that.

313
00:21:34.376 --> 00:21:37.670
Maybe there are other ways
to understand what happened.

314
00:21:38.254 --> 00:21:39.339
Yeah.

315
00:21:39.422 --> 00:21:41.591
Thomas, you are
a suicide survivor

316
00:21:41.674 --> 00:21:44.552
gifted with
a powerful imagination.

317
00:21:44.636 --> 00:21:46.388
Those facts have combined

318
00:21:46.471 --> 00:21:48.973
to create dangerous fictions
in your life.

319
00:21:49.057 --> 00:21:50.600
Yesterday,
you walked into a meeting

320
00:21:50.683 --> 00:21:51.810
with your business partner

321
00:21:51.893 --> 00:21:53.353
and he ambushed you,

322
00:21:53.436 --> 00:21:55.855
demanding you make a game
you said you would never make.

323
00:21:55.939 --> 00:21:59.275
This attack effectively
took away your voice.

324
00:21:59.359 --> 00:22:02.112
His violence triggered you
and your mind fought back.

325
00:22:02.195 --> 00:22:04.072
You did to him
what he was doing to you.

326
00:22:05.573 --> 00:22:06.950
We've talked about the value

327
00:22:07.033 --> 00:22:10.578
of adaptive anger
in healing trauma.

328
00:22:10.662 --> 00:22:14.040
Far from suggesting a repeat
of your initial breakdown,

329
00:22:14.124 --> 00:22:15.333
I believe this episode

330
00:22:15.417 --> 00:22:17.210
demonstrates healthy
self-protection.

331
00:22:18.753 --> 00:22:20.964
And more importantly,
I remember how hard

332
00:22:21.047 --> 00:22:24.092
it was for you
to share something like this.

333
00:22:24.175 --> 00:22:26.886
Which tells me
just how far we've come.

334
00:22:31.975 --> 00:22:34.269
Do you need a refill
on your prescription?

335
00:22:36.146 --> 00:22:37.313
Yeah.

336
00:22:59.919 --> 00:23:02.130
First of all, I know
I speak for everyone

337
00:23:02.213 --> 00:23:04.507
when I say that
I'm so, so excited

338
00:23:04.591 --> 00:23:06.676
to be working on a game
that was such a...

339
00:23:06.759 --> 00:23:08.845
well, game changer.

340
00:23:08.928 --> 00:23:10.513
Now, the packet
in front of you

341
00:23:10.597 --> 00:23:13.391
has our focus group research.

342
00:23:13.475 --> 00:23:14.934
Inside, you'll find
the breakdown

343
00:23:15.018 --> 00:23:17.854
including keyword association
with the brand.

344
00:23:17.937 --> 00:23:21.024
The top two being
"originality" and "fresh,"

345
00:23:21.107 --> 00:23:23.151
which I think are great things
to keep in mind

346
00:23:23.234 --> 00:23:25.445
as you begin
working on <i>Matrix 4.</i>

347
00:23:26.988 --> 00:23:28.573
And who knows how many more?

348
00:23:44.088 --> 00:23:47.509
What made <i>Matrix</i> different?
It effed with your head.

349
00:23:47.592 --> 00:23:48.885
On point.

350
00:23:48.968 --> 00:23:50.970
People want us
up in their grey space,

351
00:23:51.054 --> 00:23:54.098
switching their synaptic
"WTF" light on.

352
00:24:03.233 --> 00:24:06.569
What made <i>Matrix</i> different?
It effed with your head.

353
00:24:06.653 --> 00:24:08.488
People want us
up in their grey space,

354
00:24:08.571 --> 00:24:09.906
switching their synaptic

355
00:24:09.989 --> 00:24:12.617
"What the hell
is going on here?" light on.

356
00:24:22.710 --> 00:24:26.923
I didn't love the first one,
like some of you.

357
00:24:27.006 --> 00:24:29.425
And, frankly,
I've got zero tolerance

358
00:24:29.509 --> 00:24:31.928
for anything that requires
a syllabus and a highlighter.

359
00:24:32.011 --> 00:24:33.888
I like my games big,
loud and dumb.

360
00:24:33.972 --> 00:24:35.932
We need guns! Lots of guns.

361
00:24:36.015 --> 00:24:38.601
<i>Matrix</i> means mayhem.

362
00:24:43.273 --> 00:24:45.441
Mindless action
is not on-brand.

363
00:24:45.525 --> 00:24:46.943
She's right.

364
00:24:47.026 --> 00:24:50.071
<i>Matrix</i> is mind-porn.
Philosophy in shiny...

365
00:24:50.154 --> 00:24:51.823
- tight PVC.
- Yeah.

366
00:24:51.906 --> 00:24:53.783
Ideas are the new "sexy."

367
00:25:07.922 --> 00:25:09.632
Obviously
<i>The Matrix</i> is about...

368
00:25:09.716 --> 00:25:11.968
- ...trans-politics.
- Crypto-fascism.

369
00:25:12.051 --> 00:25:12.969
It's a metaphor...

370
00:25:13.052 --> 00:25:14.721
...of capitalist exploitation.

371
00:25:27.191 --> 00:25:31.571
This cannot be another reboot,
retread, regurgitated...

372
00:25:31.654 --> 00:25:33.740
Why not? Reboots sell.

373
00:25:36.868 --> 00:25:38.870
We are so far down the wrong
rabbit hole, here, people.

374
00:25:38.953 --> 00:25:42.790
You say <i>Matrix</i> to anyone...
You say <i>Matrix...</i>

375
00:25:42.874 --> 00:25:45.835
Matrix...
Matrix... Matrix...

376
00:25:45.918 --> 00:25:47.754
...this is what they see.

377
00:25:54.427 --> 00:25:56.721
Allow me to sum up our goal
in a single word.

378
00:25:56.804 --> 00:25:58.973
Bullet time! Bullet time!

379
00:25:59.641 --> 00:26:00.683
That's two words.

380
00:26:04.687 --> 00:26:07.857
We need
a new "bullet time."

381
00:26:10.443 --> 00:26:14.364
We need to revolutionize
gaming again.

382
00:26:14.447 --> 00:26:18.242
Revolutionize gaming
again!

383
00:26:44.143 --> 00:26:45.895
<i>Afternoon, Tiff.</i>

384
00:26:45.978 --> 00:26:47.146
The ushe?

385
00:26:47.230 --> 00:26:49.399
You know what, Skroce?
I'm going wild.

386
00:26:49.482 --> 00:26:51.984
I'll have a cortado today.

387
00:26:52.068 --> 00:26:54.612
Fly that freak flag.

388
00:26:54.696 --> 00:26:56.447
Mind if I get that?

389
00:26:56.531 --> 00:26:57.573
Oh, hi.

390
00:26:58.574 --> 00:27:00.576
Hi.

391
00:27:00.660 --> 00:27:03.162
I remember
wanting a family,

392
00:27:03.246 --> 00:27:04.539
but was that because

393
00:27:04.622 --> 00:27:07.291
that's what women
are supposed to want?

394
00:27:07.375 --> 00:27:09.085
How do you know
if you want something yourself

395
00:27:09.168 --> 00:27:12.296
or if your upbringing
programmed you to want it?

396
00:27:12.380 --> 00:27:13.381
Mmm.

397
00:27:14.424 --> 00:27:16.384
I pay my analyst
a lot of money

398
00:27:16.467 --> 00:27:19.053
to answer
such questions for me.

399
00:27:19.137 --> 00:27:20.346
Smart.

400
00:27:20.430 --> 00:27:21.639
I should get more therapy

401
00:27:21.723 --> 00:27:24.142
but honestly,
I'm too goddamn tired.

402
00:27:24.225 --> 00:27:25.977
Kids are exhausting, you know?

403
00:27:27.562 --> 00:27:29.814
No. Never had kids.

404
00:27:29.897 --> 00:27:32.650
Oh, right, I knew that.

405
00:27:32.734 --> 00:27:35.194
Sorry. I googled you.

406
00:27:37.155 --> 00:27:39.741
So, what's it like being
a world-famous game designer?

407
00:27:39.824 --> 00:27:42.368
- Must be amazing.
- Uh...

408
00:27:42.452 --> 00:27:43.953
A lot of hours.

409
00:27:44.036 --> 00:27:46.080
Sometimes it is amazing.

410
00:27:46.164 --> 00:27:47.665
Most times...

411
00:27:48.875 --> 00:27:50.168
I don't know.

412
00:27:50.251 --> 00:27:52.754
But you made <i>The Matrix.</i>
Even I've heard of that.

413
00:27:52.837 --> 00:27:56.632
Yeah. We kept
some kids entertained.

414
00:27:56.716 --> 00:27:58.843
So, worth it?

415
00:28:05.183 --> 00:28:07.769
Can I ask something
about your game?

416
00:28:07.852 --> 00:28:09.103
Sure.

417
00:28:09.187 --> 00:28:11.439
Did you base your
main character on yourself?

418
00:28:16.569 --> 00:28:18.571
There is a lot of me in him.

419
00:28:21.073 --> 00:28:24.243
Maybe a little too much.

420
00:28:26.245 --> 00:28:27.997
Can I ask you something else?

421
00:28:28.080 --> 00:28:29.290
Please.

422
00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:33.294
There's a woman in your game.

423
00:28:34.504 --> 00:28:35.505
Trinity.

424
00:28:37.340 --> 00:28:40.092
Which is a weird
coincidence also, right?

425
00:28:41.636 --> 00:28:42.762
God, yeah.

426
00:28:44.138 --> 00:28:45.389
I like her.

427
00:28:46.599 --> 00:28:48.893
- I like Trinity.
- Ah.

428
00:28:48.976 --> 00:28:50.228
And I dig her Ducati.

429
00:28:50.311 --> 00:28:53.314
Another coincidence.
I love motorcycles.

430
00:28:56.609 --> 00:28:59.320
My friend Kush and I
actually build them.

431
00:28:59.403 --> 00:29:00.530
Really?

432
00:29:00.613 --> 00:29:03.991
You have your analyst,
I have my bikes.

433
00:29:04.075 --> 00:29:08.704
So, I was looking at images
from your game. At Trinity.

434
00:29:10.414 --> 00:29:11.999
Well, I showed Chad a scene,

435
00:29:12.083 --> 00:29:14.126
and I was like,
"So, what do you think?"

436
00:29:15.211 --> 00:29:17.713
He didn't get it until I said,

437
00:29:17.797 --> 00:29:19.799
"Don't you think
she looks like me?"

438
00:29:21.634 --> 00:29:23.344
You know what he did?

439
00:29:24.679 --> 00:29:25.930
He laughed.

440
00:29:30.643 --> 00:29:33.521
And I laughed too,
like it was a joke.

441
00:29:33.604 --> 00:29:35.147
How could it not be, right?

442
00:29:37.358 --> 00:29:38.985
Made me so angry.

443
00:29:40.486 --> 00:29:42.822
I hated myself for laughing.

444
00:29:44.490 --> 00:29:47.577
I wanted to kick him so hard.

445
00:29:48.870 --> 00:29:50.162
Not too hard.

446
00:29:50.246 --> 00:29:53.457
Maybe just hard enough
to break his jaw off.

447
00:29:56.669 --> 00:29:58.504
And right now,
you're probably regretting

448
00:29:58.588 --> 00:30:00.089
sitting down with me.

449
00:30:02.258 --> 00:30:06.137
This is the best thing
I've done in a long time.

450
00:30:10.516 --> 00:30:12.226
I have to take this.

451
00:30:15.855 --> 00:30:16.939
Hi, this is Tiff.

452
00:30:17.023 --> 00:30:18.107
Oh, God, no.

453
00:30:20.151 --> 00:30:22.153
I'll be right there.

454
00:30:22.236 --> 00:30:25.072
My, uh, youngest
stuck a Lego up his nose.

455
00:30:25.990 --> 00:30:27.241
Oh.

456
00:30:28.659 --> 00:30:29.702
I gotta go.

457
00:30:31.871 --> 00:30:34.498
I hope I see you again.

458
00:30:52.433 --> 00:30:53.559
<i>There has been a report</i>

459
00:30:53.643 --> 00:30:55.144
<i>of an emergency.</i>

460
00:30:55.227 --> 00:30:57.146
<i>Proceed calmly
to the nearest exit</i>

461
00:30:57.229 --> 00:30:59.273
<i>and leave the building
immediately.</i>

462
00:30:59.357 --> 00:31:00.733
What's going on?

463
00:31:00.816 --> 00:31:02.652
We probably just got swatted
by some 14-year-old.

464
00:31:02.735 --> 00:31:04.320
Yeah, someone pissed
about the latest update.

465
00:31:04.403 --> 00:31:05.821
Or they're just a dick.

466
00:31:05.905 --> 00:31:08.658
Please move to the exits.
Building's being evacuated.

467
00:31:29.929 --> 00:31:31.597
Sir, this way.

468
00:31:37.436 --> 00:31:38.604
Jude?

469
00:31:40.106 --> 00:31:41.190
Jude!

470
00:31:47.655 --> 00:31:49.615
At last.

471
00:31:51.450 --> 00:31:52.702
Ah.

472
00:31:52.785 --> 00:31:54.245
I wasn't too sure
about the callback,

473
00:31:54.328 --> 00:31:56.330
but, you know,
it was hard to resist.

474
00:31:56.414 --> 00:31:57.540
What?

475
00:31:57.623 --> 00:31:59.041
Morpheus Uno.
Reveal at the window.

476
00:31:59.125 --> 00:32:01.585
Lightning,
thunder and theater.

477
00:32:01.669 --> 00:32:03.546
At last.

478
00:32:03.629 --> 00:32:06.048
All these years later,
here's me,

479
00:32:06.132 --> 00:32:08.384
strolling out
of a toilet stall.

480
00:32:08.467 --> 00:32:09.593
Tragedy or farce?

481
00:32:09.677 --> 00:32:11.303
I know you.

482
00:32:11.387 --> 00:32:13.389
Not every day
you meet your maker.

483
00:32:13.472 --> 00:32:14.640
This can't be happening.

484
00:32:14.724 --> 00:32:16.392
Oh, most definitely is.

485
00:32:16.475 --> 00:32:18.936
You can't be
a character I coded.

486
00:32:19.020 --> 00:32:21.063
100% natural.

487
00:32:28.529 --> 00:32:29.739
How?

488
00:32:29.822 --> 00:32:31.991
All the explanation you need.

489
00:32:35.202 --> 00:32:36.829
Oh.

490
00:32:36.912 --> 00:32:38.080
No.

491
00:32:38.164 --> 00:32:39.915
No, no, no.

492
00:32:39.999 --> 00:32:41.792
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
What do you mean, "no"?

493
00:32:41.876 --> 00:32:44.503
You wanted this, you did this.
This was your idea.

494
00:32:44.587 --> 00:32:48.924
It was a test. An experiment.

495
00:32:50.217 --> 00:32:51.427
An experiment?

496
00:32:52.970 --> 00:32:54.930
You put me
in a tiny-ass Modal,

497
00:32:55.014 --> 00:32:56.390
left me to bang my head till

498
00:32:56.474 --> 00:32:58.726
I nearly lost my shit
searching for you

499
00:32:58.809 --> 00:33:00.311
as an experiment.

500
00:33:00.394 --> 00:33:02.396
- The exit's breaking down.
- He hasn't taken the pill.

501
00:33:02.480 --> 00:33:03.814
What? There's no time.

502
00:33:03.898 --> 00:33:05.941
I know, I know.
He's having a moment.

503
00:33:06.025 --> 00:33:08.486
Does he know how hard it was
to hack that mirror?

504
00:33:10.821 --> 00:33:12.448
Still open.

505
00:33:12.531 --> 00:33:15.951
This... This can't be real.

506
00:33:16.035 --> 00:33:17.870
Target acquired.
We got him.

507
00:33:25.461 --> 00:33:26.796
This isn't happening.

508
00:33:26.879 --> 00:33:29.340
It's in my mind.
It's in my mind.

509
00:33:29.423 --> 00:33:30.633
Hey, you!
Stop! Hold it!

510
00:33:46.732 --> 00:33:48.275
This can't be happening.

511
00:33:51.403 --> 00:33:53.155
Freeze! Don't move!

512
00:34:02.123 --> 00:34:03.249
Neo!

513
00:34:18.139 --> 00:34:19.557
Oh, my God!

514
00:34:54.300 --> 00:34:55.384
Neo!

515
00:35:00.264 --> 00:35:02.474
Mr. Anderson!

516
00:35:03.309 --> 00:35:04.560
No!

517
00:35:04.643 --> 00:35:05.686
It can't be.

518
00:35:14.486 --> 00:35:16.322
I've missed you.

519
00:35:31.587 --> 00:35:33.255
It's in my mind.

520
00:35:34.381 --> 00:35:35.758
It's in my mind.

521
00:35:43.933 --> 00:35:45.434
Can you hear me, Thomas?

522
00:35:46.685 --> 00:35:49.480
Follow my voice.

523
00:35:49.563 --> 00:35:53.275
Feel the tips of your fingers.
What are they touching?

524
00:35:55.319 --> 00:35:56.695
The bell.

525
00:35:59.198 --> 00:36:00.616
Do you hear the bell?

526
00:36:04.036 --> 00:36:07.081
Do you remember what happened?
How you got here?

527
00:36:08.707 --> 00:36:10.000
You must have walked.

528
00:36:10.084 --> 00:36:11.293
I heard Deja Vu outside,

529
00:36:11.377 --> 00:36:12.628
opened my door,
and there you were.

530
00:36:17.967 --> 00:36:20.803
You feel like
you can talk about it?

531
00:36:20.886 --> 00:36:22.137
When we started
working together,

532
00:36:22.221 --> 00:36:23.973
you had lost your capacity

533
00:36:24.056 --> 00:36:26.600
to discern reality
from fiction.

534
00:36:26.684 --> 00:36:29.853
You came to me after
trying to jump off a building.

535
00:36:29.937 --> 00:36:32.231
You said you wanted
to fly away.

536
00:36:45.577 --> 00:36:48.330
We have made
a lot of progress since then,

537
00:36:48.414 --> 00:36:50.749
but you seem particularly
triggered right now.

538
00:36:50.833 --> 00:36:52.293
Can you tell me
how it started?

539
00:36:54.295 --> 00:36:56.005
He texted me.

540
00:36:57.172 --> 00:36:58.507
Who?

541
00:36:58.590 --> 00:37:00.050
Morpheus.

542
00:37:00.134 --> 00:37:01.218
Ah.

543
00:37:02.928 --> 00:37:04.305
So, he's back.

544
00:37:04.388 --> 00:37:06.557
It wasn't actually him.

545
00:37:07.725 --> 00:37:11.020
It was a program
I coded for a Modal.

546
00:37:11.103 --> 00:37:13.272
And this "Modal," Morpheus,

547
00:37:13.355 --> 00:37:15.357
came to help you escape

548
00:37:15.441 --> 00:37:19.069
from a virtual reality
called <i>The Matrix.</i>

549
00:37:29.121 --> 00:37:31.165
Am I crazy?

550
00:37:31.248 --> 00:37:33.709
We don't use that word
in here.

551
00:37:33.792 --> 00:37:36.712
What word should I use?

552
00:37:36.795 --> 00:37:40.132
What word explains
what is happening to me?

553
00:37:40.215 --> 00:37:41.884
Can I see the texts?

554
00:37:44.345 --> 00:37:45.888
They were erased.

555
00:37:51.143 --> 00:37:54.480
If we got in my car
and drove to your office,

556
00:37:54.563 --> 00:37:56.523
what do you think
we'd find there?

557
00:37:56.607 --> 00:37:57.649
Nothing.

558
00:38:00.361 --> 00:38:02.446
Because there was no attack.

559
00:38:03.655 --> 00:38:05.240
No one was killed.

560
00:38:06.158 --> 00:38:08.285
No one texted.

561
00:38:08.369 --> 00:38:10.412
My mind made it all up.

562
00:38:11.830 --> 00:38:14.500
Is that what
I'm supposed to say?

563
00:38:14.583 --> 00:38:16.085
Is that what you believe?

564
00:38:16.877 --> 00:38:18.754
It felt real.

565
00:38:18.837 --> 00:38:20.589
Of course.

566
00:38:20.672 --> 00:38:23.592
It was your great ambition
to make a game

567
00:38:23.675 --> 00:38:26.053
that was indistinguishable
from reality.

568
00:38:26.136 --> 00:38:27.596
To achieve this goal,

569
00:38:27.679 --> 00:38:30.140
you converted elements
of your life into narrative.

570
00:38:30.224 --> 00:38:32.476
Your sublimated anger
toward your business partner

571
00:38:32.559 --> 00:38:34.770
cast him as your nemesis.

572
00:38:34.853 --> 00:38:36.480
A married woman named Tiffany

573
00:38:36.563 --> 00:38:39.900
became the "Trinity"
of a doomed romance.

574
00:38:39.983 --> 00:38:44.154
Even your dislike of my cat
made it into your <i>Matrix.</i>

575
00:38:44.238 --> 00:38:46.031
There's nothing wrong
with that.

576
00:38:46.115 --> 00:38:47.574
It's what artists do.

577
00:38:47.658 --> 00:38:51.036
But it becomes a problem
when fantasies

578
00:38:51.120 --> 00:38:53.455
endanger us or other people.

579
00:38:55.707 --> 00:38:58.085
We don't want anyone
to get hurt,

580
00:38:58.168 --> 00:38:59.545
do we, Thomas?

581
00:39:07.636 --> 00:39:09.763
Hi, Thomas.
Everyone calls me "Tiff."

582
00:39:09.847 --> 00:39:12.266
- Who are you?
- My name is Trinity.

583
00:39:12.349 --> 00:39:13.976
<i>No one can tell you
you're in love.</i>

584
00:39:14.059 --> 00:39:16.562
You just know it,
through and through.

585
00:39:16.645 --> 00:39:19.148
Balls to bones.

586
00:39:19.231 --> 00:39:21.024
<i>You feel this?</i>

587
00:39:22.734 --> 00:39:24.445
I'm never letting go.

588
00:39:32.119 --> 00:39:34.163
<i>You have
to let it all go, Neo.</i>

589
00:39:34.246 --> 00:39:36.623
Free your mind.

590
00:39:55.392 --> 00:39:56.852
Huh.

591
00:39:56.935 --> 00:39:58.937
Looks easy enough.

592
00:40:05.777 --> 00:40:08.405
"Free my mind." Shit.

593
00:40:13.577 --> 00:40:15.621
Okay.

594
00:40:15.704 --> 00:40:17.122
Free my mind.

595
00:40:33.347 --> 00:40:34.890
I fly...

596
00:40:35.807 --> 00:40:37.726
or I fall.

597
00:40:45.526 --> 00:40:46.777
Who the hell are you?

598
00:40:47.653 --> 00:40:49.738
You won't remember me,

599
00:40:49.821 --> 00:40:53.075
but a long time ago,
you changed my life

600
00:40:53.158 --> 00:40:55.536
when you leapt off
another roof.

601
00:40:55.619 --> 00:40:58.539
<i>Back then, I was just like
any other coppertop,</i>

602
00:40:58.622 --> 00:41:00.332
<i>pretending my life...</i>

603
00:41:00.415 --> 00:41:04.545
until I looked up
and I saw you.

604
00:41:04.628 --> 00:41:07.130
<i>It was a different you,
but I saw</i>

605
00:41:07.923 --> 00:41:09.675
the real you,

606
00:41:09.758 --> 00:41:11.552
just a second before...

607
00:41:13.011 --> 00:41:14.096
you leapt.

608
00:41:18.850 --> 00:41:20.644
And you never fell.

609
00:41:25.941 --> 00:41:28.110
Are you the one
that hacked my Modal?

610
00:41:28.694 --> 00:41:29.695
Yeah.

611
00:41:31.196 --> 00:41:32.739
That'll be Jude.

612
00:41:32.823 --> 00:41:34.157
He's not your friend.

613
00:41:34.241 --> 00:41:35.701
He's a handle,
a program used to control you.

614
00:41:35.784 --> 00:41:36.827
He's on his way here,

615
00:41:36.910 --> 00:41:38.745
and he's bringing
Agents with him.

616
00:41:40.205 --> 00:41:41.456
Jude.

617
00:41:41.540 --> 00:41:42.958
<i>Bro, I've been calling you
all night.</i>

618
00:41:43.041 --> 00:41:44.751
<i>We have a major problemo.</i>

619
00:41:46.295 --> 00:41:47.879
Are you alone?

620
00:41:50.632 --> 00:41:53.427
<i>That's kind
of a sexy question, dude.</i>

621
00:41:53.510 --> 00:41:55.804
They don't look like
typical Agents.

622
00:41:55.887 --> 00:41:57.306
They use bots now,
skinned as normal people,

623
00:41:57.389 --> 00:41:58.515
which means they're everywhere

624
00:41:58.599 --> 00:42:00.851
and you never know
who to trust.

625
00:42:00.934 --> 00:42:02.686
Why should I trust you?

626
00:42:04.771 --> 00:42:07.858
Because if they open
that door, we lose our hack.

627
00:42:07.941 --> 00:42:09.651
I will be caught and killed

628
00:42:09.735 --> 00:42:10.944
and you will be put right back

629
00:42:11.028 --> 00:42:12.279
on that treadmill
they designed for you,

630
00:42:12.362 --> 00:42:13.488
just like they did
the last time

631
00:42:13.572 --> 00:42:14.740
you tried to leap
your way out.

632
00:42:16.074 --> 00:42:18.493
I know why you left
your Modal open.

633
00:42:18.577 --> 00:42:21.038
You needed someone else
to free Morpheus.

634
00:42:21.121 --> 00:42:23.165
And it's because of him that
we were able to get to you.

635
00:42:23.248 --> 00:42:25.125
I know these things
the same way

636
00:42:25.208 --> 00:42:27.961
that I knew one day
I would find you.

637
00:42:28.045 --> 00:42:30.672
And that when I did,
you would be ready for this.

638
00:42:35.260 --> 00:42:36.637
If you want the truth, Neo,

639
00:42:37.888 --> 00:42:39.890
you're going
to have to follow me.

640
00:42:41.433 --> 00:42:42.434
Okay.

641
00:43:01.953 --> 00:43:04.581
- Where are we?
- Tokyo.

642
00:43:04.665 --> 00:43:06.500
A moving portal
makes it harder to track us.

643
00:43:06.583 --> 00:43:09.211
- Seq is the best of them.
- Portal's clean.

644
00:43:09.294 --> 00:43:10.712
Reading our shadows.

645
00:43:12.214 --> 00:43:14.716
I don't remember this.

646
00:43:14.800 --> 00:43:17.094
We don't have to run to
phone booths anymore, either.

647
00:43:26.687 --> 00:43:28.146
Door's on your right.

648
00:43:42.369 --> 00:43:44.746
Set and setting, right?

649
00:43:44.830 --> 00:43:46.123
Oh, no.

650
00:43:46.206 --> 00:43:47.666
It's all about set

651
00:43:48.500 --> 00:43:49.751
and setting.

652
00:43:49.835 --> 00:43:51.962
After our first contact
went so badly,

653
00:43:52.045 --> 00:43:53.922
we thought elements
from your past

654
00:43:54.005 --> 00:43:55.507
might help ease you
into the present.

655
00:43:55.590 --> 00:43:58.427
Nothing comforts anxiety like

656
00:43:58.510 --> 00:43:59.928
a little nostalgia.

657
00:44:00.011 --> 00:44:02.347
This is footage
from your game.

658
00:44:09.563 --> 00:44:11.565
Time is
always against us,

659
00:44:12.441 --> 00:44:14.484
etcetera, etcetera.

660
00:44:15.694 --> 00:44:16.820
No one can be told

661
00:44:16.903 --> 00:44:20.198
what the Matrix is,
blah, blah, blah.

662
00:44:22.784 --> 00:44:24.745
You gotta see it
to believe it.

663
00:44:28.373 --> 00:44:29.958
Time to fly.

664
00:44:32.002 --> 00:44:33.462
Wait.

665
00:44:33.545 --> 00:44:34.796
If this is real,

666
00:44:34.880 --> 00:44:37.507
if I haven't lost my mind,
does that mean

667
00:44:39.217 --> 00:44:40.594
this happened?

668
00:44:49.436 --> 00:44:51.062
But if it did...

669
00:44:55.192 --> 00:44:56.735
then we died.

670
00:44:56.818 --> 00:44:58.737
Obviously not.

671
00:44:58.820 --> 00:45:00.238
Why the Machines
kept you alive

672
00:45:00.322 --> 00:45:03.200
and why they went
to such lengths to hide you

673
00:45:03.283 --> 00:45:05.118
are questions
we don't have answers to.

674
00:45:05.202 --> 00:45:06.787
Hide me?

675
00:45:06.870 --> 00:45:11.166
I've been at a company making
a game called <i>The Matrix.</i>

676
00:45:11.249 --> 00:45:13.835
Doesn't seem like they were
trying to hide anything.

677
00:45:13.919 --> 00:45:15.462
We've been tracking
that company for years.

678
00:45:15.545 --> 00:45:18.340
We screened every
Thomas Anderson we found.

679
00:45:18.423 --> 00:45:20.008
What we didn't understand

680
00:45:20.091 --> 00:45:22.594
was that they could
alter your DSI.

681
00:45:22.677 --> 00:45:24.429
Pods generate
your digital self-image

682
00:45:24.513 --> 00:45:27.015
through a feedback system
called Semblance.

683
00:45:27.098 --> 00:45:29.100
This is how
you look to yourself.

684
00:45:29.184 --> 00:45:32.896
Somehow they were able
to alter your DSI loop.

685
00:45:32.979 --> 00:45:35.482
This is how
everyone else sees you.

686
00:45:49.579 --> 00:45:51.540
Twenty years?

687
00:45:52.833 --> 00:45:56.378
Why did it take 20 years
to find me?

688
00:45:56.461 --> 00:45:58.296
It took a lot longer
than that.

689
00:45:58.380 --> 00:46:00.382
It's been over 60 years
since you and Trinity

690
00:46:00.465 --> 00:46:02.217
flew to one
of the Machine Cities.

691
00:46:02.926 --> 00:46:03.885
What?

692
00:46:03.969 --> 00:46:06.179
There's so much we don't know.

693
00:46:06.263 --> 00:46:08.014
Like why you've barely aged,

694
00:46:08.098 --> 00:46:10.308
or how many times
they've altered your DSI.

695
00:46:10.392 --> 00:46:11.726
But based on
what we do know,

696
00:46:11.810 --> 00:46:13.144
it appears no one found you

697
00:46:13.228 --> 00:46:15.063
because you didn't
want to be found.

698
00:46:15.146 --> 00:46:17.899
- That's not true.
- Maybe it isn't.

699
00:46:17.983 --> 00:46:19.192
Maybe there's no foundation

700
00:46:19.276 --> 00:46:20.443
to the rumors
that you disappeared,

701
00:46:20.527 --> 00:46:21.695
because you were working

702
00:46:21.778 --> 00:46:23.196
with the Machines
from the beginning.

703
00:46:23.280 --> 00:46:24.406
Morpheus, stop.

704
00:46:24.489 --> 00:46:27.617
All I'm saying is
this is the moment

705
00:46:27.701 --> 00:46:30.245
for you to show us
what is real.

706
00:46:30.328 --> 00:46:32.539
If you want out,

707
00:46:32.622 --> 00:46:33.999
you'll take this pill.

708
00:46:35.500 --> 00:46:37.919
But if you are
where you belong,

709
00:46:38.003 --> 00:46:40.172
you can go back to this.

710
00:46:40.255 --> 00:46:41.590
Every day.

711
00:46:41.673 --> 00:46:45.302
Over and over forever.

712
00:46:48.763 --> 00:46:49.973
Fuck.

713
00:47:00.025 --> 00:47:01.192
Keep the loop tight.

714
00:47:13.622 --> 00:47:14.789
Cybebe needs
that tower pin.

715
00:47:14.873 --> 00:47:16.750
I got a signal. It's faint.

716
00:47:16.833 --> 00:47:18.293
It's definitely off-grid.

717
00:47:25.175 --> 00:47:27.594
Captain. I'm tracking
a whole lot of weird.

718
00:47:27.677 --> 00:47:29.137
- What?
- It's some kind of graft.

719
00:47:35.393 --> 00:47:36.686
Thomas?

720
00:47:37.854 --> 00:47:39.648
Oh, God.

721
00:47:40.273 --> 00:47:41.983
Oh, no.

722
00:47:43.318 --> 00:47:45.487
- We got company.
- How'd they find us?

723
00:47:46.780 --> 00:47:49.658
Thomas, none of this is real.

724
00:47:49.741 --> 00:47:53.954
You are in the midst
of a serious psychotic break.

725
00:47:54.037 --> 00:47:56.122
- Lexy?
- Almost there.

726
00:47:56.206 --> 00:47:58.291
Thomas?

727
00:47:58.375 --> 00:48:01.211
Thomas, please.
This is not a game.

728
00:48:01.294 --> 00:48:02.796
Feel my hand.

729
00:48:02.879 --> 00:48:04.089
This is what is real.

730
00:48:07.092 --> 00:48:08.885
Stay with me.

731
00:48:08.969 --> 00:48:10.595
No. No.

732
00:48:13.473 --> 00:48:14.683
Stay with me.

733
00:48:17.352 --> 00:48:18.353
Neo!

734
00:48:22.065 --> 00:48:23.066
Morpheus!

735
00:48:24.609 --> 00:48:26.027
Let's go, let's go!

736
00:48:56.433 --> 00:48:58.518
- Bots are being activated.
- It's a swarm.

737
00:49:22.667 --> 00:49:23.752
Come on!

738
00:49:57.202 --> 00:49:58.703
I got a hack
in the bathroom. Hurry!

739
00:49:58.787 --> 00:49:59.788
Yes.

740
00:50:00.580 --> 00:50:01.581
Come on!

741
00:50:03.625 --> 00:50:04.667
Seq, where?

742
00:50:06.795 --> 00:50:08.463
- That mirror.
- What?

743
00:50:08.546 --> 00:50:10.298
- We'll never fit.
- You gotta fit,

744
00:50:10.381 --> 00:50:11.758
'cause I don't have
another way off this train.

745
00:50:11.841 --> 00:50:12.842
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

746
00:50:13.885 --> 00:50:15.386
No, no, no.

747
00:50:15.470 --> 00:50:16.638
Think "perspective."

748
00:50:16.721 --> 00:50:18.515
Closer you are,
bigger it gets.

749
00:50:22.060 --> 00:50:23.728
Okay, come on.

750
00:50:24.979 --> 00:50:26.147
In you go.

751
00:52:21.012 --> 00:52:22.388
Trinity.

752
00:52:27.727 --> 00:52:28.728
No!

753
00:53:49.600 --> 00:53:52.562
Welcome back
to the real world.

754
00:54:01.112 --> 00:54:02.280
Trinity.

755
00:54:02.363 --> 00:54:03.489
- What's up, Doc?
- His vital systems

756
00:54:03.573 --> 00:54:05.033
have been
meticulously maintained,

757
00:54:05.116 --> 00:54:06.993
but it doesn't look good.

758
00:54:12.332 --> 00:54:14.751
- We're losing him.
- Cold boot could shock him.

759
00:54:15.335 --> 00:54:16.377
Do it.

760
00:54:29.474 --> 00:54:30.975
I remember this.

761
00:54:33.644 --> 00:54:35.188
The Construct.

762
00:54:35.980 --> 00:54:38.608
In between everything

763
00:54:38.691 --> 00:54:40.818
and nothing.

764
00:54:40.902 --> 00:54:42.570
Welcome to the Crib.

765
00:54:44.155 --> 00:54:46.199
I've been chilling here
in the ship network...

766
00:54:49.577 --> 00:54:51.204
learning all about you.

767
00:54:55.917 --> 00:54:57.043
And me.

768
00:55:00.880 --> 00:55:04.717
Careful. It'll do your head in.

769
00:55:04.801 --> 00:55:08.346
Are memories turned
into fiction any less real?

770
00:55:11.516 --> 00:55:14.769
Is reality based in memory
nothing but fiction?

771
00:55:14.852 --> 00:55:18.106
As to my role in all this,
my best guess

772
00:55:18.189 --> 00:55:19.482
is that you wrote me

773
00:55:19.565 --> 00:55:21.609
as an algorithmic reflection
of two forces

774
00:55:21.692 --> 00:55:24.195
that helped you become you,

775
00:55:24.278 --> 00:55:27.740
Morpheus and Agent Smith.

776
00:55:27.824 --> 00:55:28.950
A combo pack

777
00:55:29.033 --> 00:55:31.536
of counterprogramming
that was...

778
00:55:34.330 --> 00:55:38.167
Let's just say, more than
a little bit crazy-making.

779
00:55:38.251 --> 00:55:41.170
But it worked
because here we are.

780
00:55:42.213 --> 00:55:43.798
Now, for the bad news.

781
00:55:43.881 --> 00:55:46.092
Your brain
is hooked on this shit

782
00:55:46.175 --> 00:55:49.053
the Matrix has been
force-feeding you for years.

783
00:55:49.137 --> 00:55:50.805
Hooked bad.

784
00:55:50.888 --> 00:55:52.390
You're going through
major withdrawals.

785
00:55:52.473 --> 00:55:55.685
Docbots are giving you
crap odds for surviving.

786
00:55:55.768 --> 00:55:58.020
But, see,
they don't know you like I do.

787
00:56:00.898 --> 00:56:03.109
I know exactly what you need.

788
00:56:24.964 --> 00:56:26.674
You gotta be kidding.

789
00:56:26.757 --> 00:56:27.800
Uh-uh.

790
00:56:28.801 --> 00:56:30.595
No joke.

791
00:56:30.678 --> 00:56:34.807
Could be this is the first day
of the rest of your life.

792
00:56:34.891 --> 00:56:36.726
But if you want it...

793
00:56:40.354 --> 00:56:41.689
you gotta fight for it.

794
00:56:42.815 --> 00:56:45.776
No. I'm done fighting.

795
00:56:46.819 --> 00:56:47.820
Are you?

796
00:57:31.155 --> 00:57:32.573
What the hell is he doing?

797
00:57:33.741 --> 00:57:36.536
Oh, yeah.
They taught you good.

798
00:57:41.999 --> 00:57:45.253
Made you believe their world
was all you deserved.

799
00:57:45.336 --> 00:57:47.255
But some part of you knew
that was a lie.

800
00:57:47.338 --> 00:57:50.091
Some part of you remembered
what was real.

801
00:57:52.843 --> 00:57:54.011
You don't know me.

802
00:57:54.637 --> 00:57:55.680
No?

803
00:58:01.644 --> 00:58:02.645
Ooh.

804
00:58:38.347 --> 00:58:39.974
I know you, because I know

805
00:58:40.057 --> 00:58:41.976
the only thing
that still matters to you.

806
00:58:42.059 --> 00:58:45.229
I know it's why you're here,
why you're still fighting

807
00:58:45.313 --> 00:58:46.897
and why you will
never give up.

808
00:59:01.078 --> 00:59:02.413
Come on, Neo!

809
00:59:03.831 --> 00:59:05.041
This is it.

810
00:59:07.168 --> 00:59:08.753
This is your last chance.

811
00:59:16.719 --> 00:59:18.179
You gotta fight
for your goddamn life

812
00:59:18.262 --> 00:59:19.597
if you want to see
Trinity again.

813
00:59:24.518 --> 00:59:25.895
Come on, Neo! Fight for her!

814
00:59:28.522 --> 00:59:31.150
- Holy shit.
- Fight for her!

815
01:00:23.202 --> 01:00:24.912
- Hey.
- Hey.

816
01:00:26.831 --> 01:00:28.332
Mind if I...

817
01:00:41.512 --> 01:00:43.013
How are you doing?

818
01:00:44.557 --> 01:00:46.684
If this plug is actually real,

819
01:00:48.644 --> 01:00:50.980
that means
they took my life...

820
01:00:53.524 --> 01:00:55.901
and turned it
into a video game.

821
01:00:59.029 --> 01:01:00.656
How am I doing?

822
01:01:01.615 --> 01:01:03.659
I don't know.

823
01:01:03.743 --> 01:01:05.911
I don't even know how to know.

824
01:01:07.037 --> 01:01:08.497
That's it, isn't it?

825
01:01:09.999 --> 01:01:12.209
If we don't know
what's real...

826
01:01:14.295 --> 01:01:15.421
we can't resist.

827
01:01:18.340 --> 01:01:19.800
They took your story,

828
01:01:19.884 --> 01:01:21.385
something that meant

829
01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:24.722
so much to people like me,

830
01:01:26.348 --> 01:01:29.018
and turned it
into something trivial.

831
01:01:30.811 --> 01:01:32.605
That's what the Matrix does.

832
01:01:33.439 --> 01:01:35.649
It weaponizes every idea.

833
01:01:36.400 --> 01:01:37.818
Every dream.

834
01:01:39.320 --> 01:01:41.113
Everything
that's important to us.

835
01:01:43.574 --> 01:01:45.868
Where better to bury truth
than inside something

836
01:01:45.951 --> 01:01:48.996
as ordinary as a video game?

837
01:01:49.079 --> 01:01:51.081
That sounds like the Oracle.

838
01:01:52.500 --> 01:01:54.293
Heard so much about her.

839
01:01:57.087 --> 01:01:58.631
She was gone
before I was free.

840
01:02:00.257 --> 01:02:01.675
Gone?

841
01:02:01.759 --> 01:02:04.595
When this new version
of the Matrix was uploaded,

842
01:02:06.096 --> 01:02:07.640
there was a purge.

843
01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:16.273
They promised peace
and they gave us purge.

844
01:02:17.733 --> 01:02:19.193
No.

845
01:02:19.276 --> 01:02:20.986
No, there was peace.

846
01:02:22.404 --> 01:02:27.535
You made it possible,
and it changed everything.

847
01:02:27.618 --> 01:02:31.121
Doesn't feel like
it changed anything.

848
01:02:31.205 --> 01:02:34.416
The Matrix is
the same or worse.

849
01:02:34.500 --> 01:02:36.710
And I'm back where I started.

850
01:02:39.463 --> 01:02:41.924
It feels like
everything I did,

851
01:02:42.967 --> 01:02:44.468
everything we did...

852
01:02:50.474 --> 01:02:52.685
...like none of it mattered.

853
01:02:54.895 --> 01:02:56.564
All of it mattered.

854
01:02:58.315 --> 01:02:59.817
I can show you.

855
01:03:10.494 --> 01:03:12.079
This is my crew.

856
01:03:15.207 --> 01:03:17.376
Our operator, Seq.

857
01:03:19.587 --> 01:03:23.465
Sequoia. But everybody
calls me Seq.

858
01:03:23.549 --> 01:03:25.009
Nice to meet you.

859
01:03:26.051 --> 01:03:28.095
Dad loved redwoods.

860
01:03:28.178 --> 01:03:29.430
When he escaped the Matrix

861
01:03:29.513 --> 01:03:31.056
and found out
they no longer existed,

862
01:03:31.140 --> 01:03:32.641
it almost killed him.

863
01:03:32.725 --> 01:03:33.934
Lucky, he met Mom

864
01:03:34.810 --> 01:03:36.437
and here I am.

865
01:03:36.520 --> 01:03:40.232
This is Lexy,
Berg and Ellster.

866
01:03:40.983 --> 01:03:42.109
Hi.

867
01:03:42.192 --> 01:03:44.778
You knew my grandfather,
Captain Roland.

868
01:03:44.862 --> 01:03:47.323
Roland was your grandfather?

869
01:03:48.115 --> 01:03:49.199
He always laughed,

870
01:03:49.283 --> 01:03:50.242
joking how he never
believed in you.

871
01:03:51.368 --> 01:03:52.786
But, in private, he said that

872
01:03:52.870 --> 01:03:54.997
you freed his mind
a second time.

873
01:03:55.080 --> 01:03:57.124
Uh, not to fanboy out here,

874
01:03:57.207 --> 01:03:59.209
but this is kind
of a huge moment for me.

875
01:03:59.293 --> 01:04:01.795
Berg is our resident
Neo-ologist.

876
01:04:01.879 --> 01:04:03.088
A what?

877
01:04:03.172 --> 01:04:06.216
There's a lot of people
out there like me

878
01:04:06.300 --> 01:04:08.636
who are a little bit
obsessed with your life.

879
01:04:08.719 --> 01:04:09.887
I would never have recognized

880
01:04:09.970 --> 01:04:11.096
your Modal
if it weren't for him.

881
01:04:11.180 --> 01:04:12.431
Whenever
you're feeling up for it,

882
01:04:12.514 --> 01:04:14.475
I've got, like,
a million questions.

883
01:04:14.558 --> 01:04:17.019
Me too. Starting with them.

884
01:04:18.354 --> 01:04:19.396
It's okay.

885
01:04:20.147 --> 01:04:21.398
Come meet him.

886
01:04:21.482 --> 01:04:22.775
This is Cybebe.

887
01:04:22.858 --> 01:04:24.276
That's Octacles.

888
01:04:24.360 --> 01:04:27.029
That's Lumin8.

889
01:04:27.112 --> 01:04:29.365
Machines are on our side now?

890
01:04:29.448 --> 01:04:30.658
They are synthients.

891
01:04:30.741 --> 01:04:32.409
It's a word
they prefer to "Machines."

892
01:04:32.493 --> 01:04:33.827
Your contact
with the Synthient City

893
01:04:33.911 --> 01:04:36.288
had a huge impact
on their world.

894
01:04:36.372 --> 01:04:37.498
That's what I meant.

895
01:04:37.581 --> 01:04:38.832
What you changed

896
01:04:38.916 --> 01:04:40.501
that nobody believed
could ever be changed.

897
01:04:42.419 --> 01:04:44.922
The meaning of "our side."

898
01:04:48.717 --> 01:04:50.552
Cybebe and Octacles
risked their lives

899
01:04:50.636 --> 01:04:51.804
to help get you out.

900
01:04:53.263 --> 01:04:54.264
Thank you.

901
01:04:55.808 --> 01:04:56.850
But why?

902
01:04:56.934 --> 01:04:59.478
Not all seek to control.

903
01:04:59.561 --> 01:05:01.563
Just as not all
wish to be free.

904
01:05:03.357 --> 01:05:04.608
What is that?

905
01:05:04.692 --> 01:05:06.986
An exomorphic-particle codex.
It's pretty new.

906
01:05:07.069 --> 01:05:09.196
It gives programs
access to this world.

907
01:05:09.279 --> 01:05:10.489
Within limits.

908
01:05:10.572 --> 01:05:13.575
Limits are the domain
of the limited.

909
01:05:13.659 --> 01:05:15.202
Morpheus.

910
01:05:15.285 --> 01:05:16.328
Thank you.

911
01:05:16.412 --> 01:05:17.830
It was my honor.

912
01:05:19.623 --> 01:05:20.874
Wow.

913
01:05:20.958 --> 01:05:22.126
How does it work?

914
01:05:22.209 --> 01:05:23.711
Paramagnetic oscillation.

915
01:05:23.794 --> 01:05:24.962
If you want,

916
01:05:25.045 --> 01:05:26.296
I can download
the codex manual for you.

917
01:05:26.380 --> 01:05:28.799
- Sure.
- Downloading used to be fun.

918
01:05:28.882 --> 01:05:31.260
Now it's all manuals
and diagnostics.

919
01:05:31.343 --> 01:05:33.053
Can I ask them something?

920
01:05:35.973 --> 01:05:39.226
When you unplugged me,
there was another pod?

921
01:05:40.561 --> 01:05:43.439
Yes. We've analyzed the data.

922
01:05:44.648 --> 01:05:45.983
It could be Trinity.

923
01:05:46.817 --> 01:05:48.402
It's her.

924
01:05:48.485 --> 01:05:51.572
I figured we were going
to have this conversation.

925
01:05:51.655 --> 01:05:54.575
Look, you were not
a typical flush-and-grab.

926
01:05:54.658 --> 01:05:56.326
You were in this weird tower
that Cybebe

927
01:05:56.410 --> 01:05:58.495
had never accessed,
and she's now exiled.

928
01:05:58.579 --> 01:06:00.956
We burned
our one shot for you.

929
01:06:01.040 --> 01:06:03.083
Even if it were Trinity
and she wanted to be free,

930
01:06:03.167 --> 01:06:05.210
we have no idea how to do it.

931
01:06:05.294 --> 01:06:06.295
Yet.

932
01:06:08.714 --> 01:06:11.592
Nobody believed
we'd ever find him,

933
01:06:11.675 --> 01:06:12.718
but we did.

934
01:06:15.137 --> 01:06:17.056
Okay.

935
01:06:17.139 --> 01:06:20.267
We don't know
how to get her out... yet.

936
01:06:22.311 --> 01:06:24.980
Captain, we're approaching
security clearance.

937
01:06:26.273 --> 01:06:27.441
We're here.

938
01:06:27.524 --> 01:06:28.567
Zion?

939
01:06:36.658 --> 01:06:38.118
Have a seat.

940
01:06:38.202 --> 01:06:40.954
This is Hanno.
Best pilot in our fleet.

941
01:06:41.038 --> 01:06:41.997
Quite a few synthients

942
01:06:42.081 --> 01:06:43.540
deserve that title before me.

943
01:06:43.624 --> 01:06:44.792
Mnemosyne, <i>you are cleared</i>

944
01:06:44.875 --> 01:06:46.251
<i>for landing. Welcome home.</i>

945
01:06:46.335 --> 01:06:48.003
Thank you, Control.

946
01:06:48.087 --> 01:06:49.671
Um, we're about to crash.

947
01:06:56.595 --> 01:06:57.846
General realized we were

948
01:06:57.930 --> 01:06:59.973
never going to beat
the Sentinels, so...

949
01:07:00.057 --> 01:07:02.184
we just got better
at hiding from them.

950
01:07:06.772 --> 01:07:08.357
Welcome to Io.

951
01:07:09.983 --> 01:07:11.401
Io.

952
01:07:17.825 --> 01:07:20.577
Wow. That looks real.

953
01:07:21.078 --> 01:07:22.663
Bio-sky.

954
01:07:26.250 --> 01:07:28.585
Works kind of like
grow lights.

955
01:07:28.669 --> 01:07:30.337
It's way more complex
than that.

956
01:07:30.420 --> 01:07:32.881
It pulls water from the crust,
hydronating the air.

957
01:07:32.965 --> 01:07:36.301
It balances the ECO
and our SRI cycles.

958
01:07:37.386 --> 01:07:38.720
Plus...

959
01:07:39.555 --> 01:07:41.348
it is pretty to look at.

960
01:07:41.431 --> 01:07:43.225
As opposed to that.

961
01:07:44.518 --> 01:07:47.104
I guess the general sent us
a welcome party.

962
01:08:05.372 --> 01:08:06.790
God damn.

963
01:08:07.875 --> 01:08:09.084
It is you.

964
01:08:09.960 --> 01:08:11.128
Niobe?

965
01:08:12.963 --> 01:08:16.550
A few more wrinkles
and a few less teeth,

966
01:08:16.633 --> 01:08:20.304
but wise enough to know
I don't know anything.

967
01:08:20.387 --> 01:08:23.056
I sure as shit
never saw this coming.

968
01:08:23.891 --> 01:08:25.058
Neither did I.

969
01:08:25.142 --> 01:08:26.476
I told you he was alive.

970
01:08:26.560 --> 01:08:28.520
Captain, you and your crew
have been grounded.

971
01:08:28.604 --> 01:08:30.230
General,
if you'd just let me explain.

972
01:08:30.314 --> 01:08:32.941
The protocols are put in place
for everyone's protection.

973
01:08:33.025 --> 01:08:34.902
I'm sorry.
I saw an opportunity

974
01:08:34.985 --> 01:08:36.445
and I was afraid
we'd lose him.

975
01:08:36.528 --> 01:08:39.198
But, General, people have been
waiting for so long.

976
01:08:40.866 --> 01:08:42.117
We found The One.

977
01:08:43.952 --> 01:08:45.662
I don't believe in The One.

978
01:08:47.915 --> 01:08:49.041
I never did.

979
01:08:49.708 --> 01:08:50.792
No?

980
01:08:51.877 --> 01:08:53.420
Me neither.

981
01:08:53.503 --> 01:08:55.881
But there was a time

982
01:08:55.964 --> 01:08:58.634
when you trusted me
with your ship,

983
01:08:58.717 --> 01:09:00.510
against the Council's orders.

984
01:09:00.594 --> 01:09:02.679
The world was different then.

985
01:09:04.514 --> 01:09:06.141
We were different.

986
01:09:08.185 --> 01:09:09.603
Report to the docks.

987
01:09:09.686 --> 01:09:11.396
Scrub down the <i>Mnemosyne.</i>

988
01:09:11.480 --> 01:09:13.774
Transfer your access codes.

989
01:09:13.857 --> 01:09:15.275
You are done, Captain.

990
01:09:24.952 --> 01:09:26.787
We need to talk.

991
01:09:32.000 --> 01:09:34.670
When word first came

992
01:09:34.753 --> 01:09:37.005
that it actually
might be you...

993
01:09:40.759 --> 01:09:44.554
I didn't know how I would feel
in this moment.

994
01:09:52.437 --> 01:09:54.398
It is nice to see you.

995
01:09:54.481 --> 01:09:57.192
It's good to see you too.

996
01:10:03.073 --> 01:10:05.826
A long way
from Dozer's paint stripper.

997
01:10:05.909 --> 01:10:08.870
Yes.

998
01:10:08.954 --> 01:10:10.706
A lot has changed.

999
01:10:12.249 --> 01:10:14.167
Except maybe you.

1000
01:10:16.962 --> 01:10:18.505
You remember this?

1001
01:10:25.595 --> 01:10:28.348
It's so easy to forget
how much noise

1002
01:10:28.432 --> 01:10:30.350
the Matrix pumps
into your head

1003
01:10:30.434 --> 01:10:32.227
until you unplug.

1004
01:10:33.687 --> 01:10:35.063
Yeah.

1005
01:10:35.147 --> 01:10:38.066
Something else
makes the same kind of noise.

1006
01:10:38.150 --> 01:10:40.360
Takes over every damn thing,

1007
01:10:40.444 --> 01:10:42.154
just like the Matrix.

1008
01:10:43.822 --> 01:10:44.823
War.

1009
01:10:46.533 --> 01:10:49.161
I stood at the barricade
of the Temple.

1010
01:10:50.954 --> 01:10:53.248
Staring
at the army of Sentinels,

1011
01:10:54.374 --> 01:10:57.002
waiting for them
to kill every one of us.

1012
01:10:58.462 --> 01:11:01.548
But then, they left.

1013
01:11:02.758 --> 01:11:05.218
They said you saved us.

1014
01:11:05.302 --> 01:11:06.470
I didn't believe it.

1015
01:11:06.553 --> 01:11:09.890
Every night I would dream
of attack sirens.

1016
01:11:10.557 --> 01:11:11.808
But then,

1017
01:11:14.394 --> 01:11:16.605
I would wake up to this...

1018
01:11:20.609 --> 01:11:22.069
silence.

1019
01:11:25.530 --> 01:11:27.074
I'm ashamed of it now.

1020
01:11:27.157 --> 01:11:31.161
My pessimism of how long
it took me to believe

1021
01:11:31.244 --> 01:11:34.498
a world without war
was possible.

1022
01:11:35.916 --> 01:11:37.918
You gave me that.

1023
01:11:38.001 --> 01:11:40.879
You gave that gift to us all.

1024
01:11:40.962 --> 01:11:44.633
And it is the gift
that continues to bear fruit.

1025
01:11:47.344 --> 01:11:49.096
Come help me get up.

1026
01:11:49.179 --> 01:11:50.931
Let's take a walk.

1027
01:12:15.038 --> 01:12:17.040
Oh! Beautiful.

1028
01:12:18.125 --> 01:12:21.086
This is Freya, head of botany.

1029
01:12:21.169 --> 01:12:24.464
And this is Quillion,
our lead digitologist.

1030
01:12:24.548 --> 01:12:28.552
I presume our guest
needs no introduction.

1031
01:12:28.635 --> 01:12:31.304
Nothing travels
faster than light,

1032
01:12:31.388 --> 01:12:32.639
except gossip.

1033
01:12:35.016 --> 01:12:36.435
Welcome to the Garden, Neo.

1034
01:12:38.478 --> 01:12:39.646
A strawberry?

1035
01:12:39.729 --> 01:12:41.440
Using digital code
from the Matrix,

1036
01:12:41.523 --> 01:12:43.942
we retro-convert it
into DNA sequences.

1037
01:12:44.025 --> 01:12:45.444
And they grow here?

1038
01:12:45.527 --> 01:12:47.154
It's not easy
augmenting the genome

1039
01:12:47.237 --> 01:12:49.781
to photosynthesize
Bio-sky, but...

1040
01:12:49.865 --> 01:12:51.616
We're getting there.

1041
01:12:52.367 --> 01:12:54.077
Go ahead. Try it.

1042
01:13:01.585 --> 01:13:03.795
We're quite excited
about the blueberries.

1043
01:13:03.879 --> 01:13:05.797
You remember that shit
we used to eat?

1044
01:13:05.881 --> 01:13:08.258
That slop
that tasted like rust.

1045
01:13:09.843 --> 01:13:13.472
Zion could have never
made something like this.

1046
01:13:13.555 --> 01:13:15.182
Why?

1047
01:13:15.265 --> 01:13:17.851
Because we needed synthients

1048
01:13:17.934 --> 01:13:19.895
and DI like him.

1049
01:13:19.978 --> 01:13:23.356
Zion was stuck in the past.
Stuck in war.

1050
01:13:23.440 --> 01:13:25.817
Stuck in a Matrix of its own.

1051
01:13:25.901 --> 01:13:29.779
They believed
that it had to be us or them.

1052
01:13:29.863 --> 01:13:32.866
This city was built by us

1053
01:13:32.949 --> 01:13:34.618
and them.

1054
01:13:40.290 --> 01:13:41.833
What happened to Zion?

1055
01:13:41.917 --> 01:13:45.337
I've been waiting
for you to ask that question.

1056
01:13:47.297 --> 01:13:50.759
All of the troubles
started in the Machine Cities.

1057
01:13:50.842 --> 01:13:54.554
Power plants were unable
to produce enough energy.

1058
01:13:54.638 --> 01:13:58.391
Nothing can breed violence
like scarcity.

1059
01:14:00.143 --> 01:14:01.728
For the first time,

1060
01:14:01.811 --> 01:14:05.023
<i>we saw machines at war
with one other.</i>

1061
01:14:08.026 --> 01:14:12.030
We got word from the Oracle
of a new power rising.

1062
01:14:13.990 --> 01:14:16.660
That was the last
we heard from her.

1063
01:14:20.330 --> 01:14:21.706
Morpheus.

1064
01:14:21.790 --> 01:14:26.169
After the siege,
he was elected unanimously.

1065
01:14:26.253 --> 01:14:29.130
High Chair of the Council.

1066
01:14:29.214 --> 01:14:32.634
Oh, how he loved that.

1067
01:14:32.717 --> 01:14:36.930
But as rumors
of this new power spread,

1068
01:14:37.013 --> 01:14:38.431
he ignored them.

1069
01:14:38.515 --> 01:14:43.144
He was certain what you had
done could not be undone.

1070
01:14:43.228 --> 01:14:47.190
All of these people never
stopped believing in miracles,

1071
01:14:47.274 --> 01:14:49.651
believing in you.

1072
01:15:01.705 --> 01:15:03.081
I'm sorry.

1073
01:15:04.916 --> 01:15:07.335
How could I know
this would happen?

1074
01:15:07.419 --> 01:15:09.713
We didn't understand
all of it back then.

1075
01:15:09.796 --> 01:15:11.631
No more than we do now.

1076
01:15:11.715 --> 01:15:15.010
I didn't come here
to cause you problems, Niobe,

1077
01:15:16.052 --> 01:15:17.804
but I need your help.

1078
01:15:19.472 --> 01:15:20.932
Trinity is alive.

1079
01:15:21.016 --> 01:15:22.767
Then there is
another question.

1080
01:15:22.851 --> 01:15:24.644
Why did they keep her alive?

1081
01:15:24.728 --> 01:15:25.979
I can't answer that.

1082
01:15:26.062 --> 01:15:29.399
But if there's a chance
I can free her,

1083
01:15:29.482 --> 01:15:31.026
I have to try.

1084
01:15:31.109 --> 01:15:35.030
Even if it means endangering
everyone in this city?

1085
01:15:39.284 --> 01:15:40.994
I'm sorry, Neo.

1086
01:15:41.077 --> 01:15:44.748
I won't let what happened
to Zion happen to Io.

1087
01:15:46.541 --> 01:15:47.917
I hope you'll forgive
an old woman

1088
01:15:48.001 --> 01:15:51.087
for asking you to go
with Sheperd, here,

1089
01:15:51.171 --> 01:15:52.672
till we have
better understanding

1090
01:15:52.756 --> 01:15:54.174
of what's going on.

1091
01:15:54.257 --> 01:15:57.302
You're going to imprison me
after I just got free?

1092
01:15:57.385 --> 01:16:01.181
I know it doesn't seem fair,

1093
01:16:01.264 --> 01:16:04.059
but neither does growing old.

1094
01:16:04.142 --> 01:16:06.269
But you don't
hear me complaining.

1095
01:16:18.281 --> 01:16:20.116
Sorry.

1096
01:16:20.200 --> 01:16:22.243
I've never met
a legend before.

1097
01:16:25.622 --> 01:16:26.706
Neo.

1098
01:16:27.999 --> 01:16:29.751
Sheperd.

1099
01:16:31.127 --> 01:16:32.962
Crazy. You're real.

1100
01:16:34.923 --> 01:16:36.049
"Real."

1101
01:16:37.133 --> 01:16:39.135
There's that word again.

1102
01:16:44.641 --> 01:16:47.018
People talk a lot
about the old days.

1103
01:16:47.102 --> 01:16:49.354
About you, the viral Agent.

1104
01:16:49.437 --> 01:16:52.065
The siege of Zion.

1105
01:16:52.148 --> 01:16:54.150
Everything was simpler
back then.

1106
01:16:55.151 --> 01:16:56.736
People wanted to be free.

1107
01:16:58.822 --> 01:17:00.740
It's different now.

1108
01:17:00.824 --> 01:17:04.285
Sometimes it feels like
people gave up.

1109
01:17:05.537 --> 01:17:07.247
Like the Matrix won.

1110
01:17:10.041 --> 01:17:11.459
This is you.

1111
01:17:15.463 --> 01:17:17.757
And I gotta ask you one thing.

1112
01:17:19.801 --> 01:17:21.511
Is it true you could fly?

1113
01:17:26.349 --> 01:17:27.350
Cool.

1114
01:17:57.881 --> 01:17:59.174
Morpheus.

1115
01:17:59.257 --> 01:18:02.177
Oh. General stuck you
in the Rapunzel tower.

1116
01:18:04.637 --> 01:18:06.139
On the upside,
it's a nice view.

1117
01:18:06.222 --> 01:18:08.308
What happened to Bugs
and the others?

1118
01:18:08.391 --> 01:18:10.101
They're supposed to be
sterilizing the <i>Mnemosyne</i>

1119
01:18:10.185 --> 01:18:12.312
- with a toothbrush.
- "Supposed to be"?

1120
01:18:12.395 --> 01:18:13.730
Well, I could tell you
that they're standing by,

1121
01:18:13.813 --> 01:18:15.064
waiting for you
to make the choice

1122
01:18:15.148 --> 01:18:16.983
to remain meekly incarcerated

1123
01:18:17.067 --> 01:18:19.402
or bust the hell out of here
and go and find Trinity.

1124
01:18:20.987 --> 01:18:22.072
But that ain't a choice.

1125
01:18:34.709 --> 01:18:36.836
General,
what should we do?

1126
01:18:40.256 --> 01:18:42.842
Bugs has the same
independence of mind

1127
01:18:42.926 --> 01:18:44.385
she had the day you freed her.

1128
01:18:44.469 --> 01:18:47.472
This is not
independence of mind.

1129
01:18:47.555 --> 01:18:48.598
It's mutiny.

1130
01:18:49.933 --> 01:18:51.184
Come on, 'Be.

1131
01:18:51.267 --> 01:18:54.270
I know how much
you hated locking him up.

1132
01:18:54.354 --> 01:18:57.065
Just like I know
there's a part of you

1133
01:18:57.148 --> 01:19:00.193
that's relieved now
that he's gone.

1134
01:19:01.653 --> 01:19:05.490
We've worked so hard
to keep Io safe.

1135
01:19:08.243 --> 01:19:09.869
This scares me.

1136
01:19:20.421 --> 01:19:21.714
That's her.

1137
01:19:21.798 --> 01:19:22.924
On the bridge.

1138
01:19:23.466 --> 01:19:24.467
Got her.

1139
01:19:33.143 --> 01:19:35.395
It's sick
how the Semblance works.

1140
01:19:35.478 --> 01:19:38.231
You see flashes
of the real her, but...

1141
01:19:38.314 --> 01:19:39.941
the way she reads...

1142
01:19:41.651 --> 01:19:44.279
Code-wise,
she's pure bluepill.

1143
01:19:46.155 --> 01:19:49.242
This is a tough question, Neo,
but it has to be asked.

1144
01:19:50.368 --> 01:19:52.537
What if she's happy
where she is?

1145
01:19:53.997 --> 01:19:55.248
How did I read?

1146
01:19:57.333 --> 01:19:59.252
Exactly like her.

1147
01:20:03.006 --> 01:20:05.258
Take us to broadcast depth.

1148
01:20:16.561 --> 01:20:18.021
Thank you for helping me.

1149
01:20:19.647 --> 01:20:21.649
Most of us are here
because of you.

1150
01:20:24.319 --> 01:20:25.445
I also admit our only chance

1151
01:20:25.528 --> 01:20:26.946
to get out
of the general's doghouse

1152
01:20:27.030 --> 01:20:28.656
is for you to find your mojo.

1153
01:20:30.366 --> 01:20:32.952
What if I can't be
what I once was?

1154
01:20:34.495 --> 01:20:36.122
Then we're all fucked.

1155
01:20:36.205 --> 01:20:37.582
Two minutes.

1156
01:20:37.665 --> 01:20:39.042
Two minutes to broadcast.

1157
01:20:48.217 --> 01:20:49.552
I slipped you in
through a hotel room.

1158
01:20:51.387 --> 01:20:52.847
Should be safe.

1159
01:21:03.650 --> 01:21:05.151
Portal's open.

1160
01:21:05.234 --> 01:21:07.362
Closest I could get you is
the warehouse near her garage.

1161
01:21:07.445 --> 01:21:08.988
Whole zone's
crawling with bots.

1162
01:21:10.365 --> 01:21:11.908
Let's go.

1163
01:21:39.143 --> 01:21:42.271
So, what do you think of him?

1164
01:21:42.355 --> 01:21:45.149
I was kinda worried at first
because he's so much older.

1165
01:21:45.233 --> 01:21:47.735
The beard, the hair... Oh.

1166
01:21:47.819 --> 01:21:51.239
- No, totally works for me.
- You idiot.

1167
01:21:51.322 --> 01:21:52.699
I mean "The One" thing.

1168
01:21:54.367 --> 01:21:57.328
You know, everyone that
shipped with him died.

1169
01:21:57.412 --> 01:22:00.206
Oh, yeah. He's gonna
get us all killed, for sure.

1170
01:22:05.586 --> 01:22:07.130
Predictable as ever.

1171
01:22:09.382 --> 01:22:11.134
Smith.

1172
01:22:11.217 --> 01:22:13.553
Smith? As in, "the" Smith?

1173
01:22:21.686 --> 01:22:22.979
This is so insane.

1174
01:22:23.062 --> 01:22:24.313
There's so many theories
about the two of them

1175
01:22:24.397 --> 01:22:26.065
and they're standing
right there.

1176
01:22:26.149 --> 01:22:27.734
This code is freaky!

1177
01:22:27.817 --> 01:22:30.695
He's like an Agent, but not.

1178
01:22:34.866 --> 01:22:36.451
An appeal to reason.

1179
01:22:40.663 --> 01:22:42.165
How did you find us?

1180
01:22:42.248 --> 01:22:45.168
You never appreciated
our relationship.

1181
01:22:45.251 --> 01:22:46.627
Not like The Analyst.

1182
01:22:46.711 --> 01:22:48.629
- The what?
- My doctor.

1183
01:22:48.713 --> 01:22:52.425
He used our bond
and turned it into a chain.

1184
01:22:52.508 --> 01:22:54.177
It's so obvious
once you see it, right?

1185
01:22:54.260 --> 01:22:57.680
But this whole altered-code
update really blew my mind.

1186
01:22:57.764 --> 01:22:59.766
I still don't know
how he did it.

1187
01:22:59.849 --> 01:23:02.643
You, as a balding nerd.

1188
01:23:02.727 --> 01:23:04.479
Hilarious.

1189
01:23:04.562 --> 01:23:06.939
And me...

1190
01:23:07.023 --> 01:23:09.692
even more perfect.

1191
01:23:09.776 --> 01:23:11.778
Maybe a little too far
on the piercing blue eyes.

1192
01:23:11.861 --> 01:23:13.780
What do you think?

1193
01:23:13.863 --> 01:23:15.823
What do you want, Smith?

1194
01:23:17.992 --> 01:23:20.286
I have such dreams, Tom.

1195
01:23:20.369 --> 01:23:22.080
Big dreams.

1196
01:23:22.163 --> 01:23:24.916
Well, mostly just extremely
violent revenge fantasies,

1197
01:23:24.999 --> 01:23:26.417
but in order for me
to pursue mine,

1198
01:23:26.501 --> 01:23:28.544
I need to dissuade you
from pursuing yours.

1199
01:23:28.628 --> 01:23:32.256
Hmm. Sounds like conflict.

1200
01:23:33.966 --> 01:23:35.510
Inevitable?

1201
01:23:36.719 --> 01:23:38.054
Doesn't have to be.

1202
01:23:38.137 --> 01:23:40.306
All you have to do
is stay out of the Matrix,

1203
01:23:40.389 --> 01:23:41.891
and leave
the good doctor to me.

1204
01:23:41.974 --> 01:23:44.310
You can have him.
I'm here for Trinity.

1205
01:23:44.393 --> 01:23:45.895
That's the trouble, Tom.

1206
01:23:45.978 --> 01:23:48.648
He knew you'd come,
just like I did.

1207
01:23:50.399 --> 01:23:51.609
Trust me.

1208
01:23:52.568 --> 01:23:54.112
You're not ready for him.

1209
01:23:54.195 --> 01:23:56.989
Captain, I'm reading portals
from the lower frequencies.

1210
01:24:02.286 --> 01:24:05.456
I won't have his leash
on my neck again.

1211
01:24:12.922 --> 01:24:15.174
I found some
old acquaintances of yours.

1212
01:24:16.217 --> 01:24:19.595
Bugs!

1213
01:24:33.276 --> 01:24:34.318
Exiles.

1214
01:24:34.402 --> 01:24:35.570
I thought
they were all purged.

1215
01:24:35.653 --> 01:24:37.155
You?

1216
01:24:37.238 --> 01:24:38.364
Oh!

1217
01:24:38.447 --> 01:24:40.783
It is you!

1218
01:24:42.118 --> 01:24:45.705
All these years.
I can't believe it.

1219
01:24:46.372 --> 01:24:48.040
Oh, God.

1220
01:24:48.124 --> 01:24:52.086
You stole my life!

1221
01:24:56.841 --> 01:24:58.384
What the Merv
is trying to say,

1222
01:24:58.467 --> 01:25:00.928
is that their situation
is a little bit like mine.

1223
01:25:01.012 --> 01:25:03.222
To have their lives back,
yours has to end.

1224
01:25:06.893 --> 01:25:07.977
Kill him!

1225
01:25:21.199 --> 01:25:23.659
You ruined

1226
01:25:23.743 --> 01:25:26.871
every suck-my-silky-ass thing!

1227
01:25:26.954 --> 01:25:29.540
We had grace.

1228
01:25:34.587 --> 01:25:36.130
We had style!

1229
01:25:36.214 --> 01:25:38.216
We had conversation!

1230
01:25:38.299 --> 01:25:40.259
Not this...

1231
01:26:04.784 --> 01:26:08.329
Art, films,
books were all better!

1232
01:26:08.412 --> 01:26:11.624
Originality mattered!

1233
01:26:11.707 --> 01:26:13.626
You gave us
Face-Zucker-suck

1234
01:26:13.709 --> 01:26:17.171
and Cock-me-climatey-
Wiki-piss-and-shit!

1235
01:27:03.301 --> 01:27:04.885
I still know kung fu.

1236
01:27:06.762 --> 01:27:07.763
Neo!

1237
01:27:37.460 --> 01:27:38.961
Just like old times.

1238
01:28:36.602 --> 01:28:37.645
Neo.

1239
01:28:39.563 --> 01:28:42.233
I've been thinking
about us, Tom.

1240
01:28:42.316 --> 01:28:45.611
Look how binary is the form,
the nature of things.

1241
01:28:46.862 --> 01:28:48.155
Ones and zeros.

1242
01:28:49.365 --> 01:28:50.491
Light and dark.

1243
01:28:52.618 --> 01:28:54.662
Choice and its absence.

1244
01:28:58.040 --> 01:29:00.292
Anderson and Smith.

1245
01:29:36.912 --> 01:29:39.123
You've lost something, Tom.

1246
01:29:43.085 --> 01:29:44.920
You're not
what you used to be.

1247
01:29:46.172 --> 01:29:47.256
It's true.

1248
01:30:00.603 --> 01:30:02.605
- Nice one.
- Thanks.

1249
01:30:10.446 --> 01:30:11.655
Come on, Neo.

1250
01:30:36.639 --> 01:30:39.183
Captain. You okay?

1251
01:30:39.266 --> 01:30:42.228
Yeah. Where's Neo?

1252
01:30:42.311 --> 01:30:43.437
Smith is killing him.

1253
01:30:43.521 --> 01:30:44.897
Where?

1254
01:30:52.404 --> 01:30:54.406
I feel bad about this, Tom.

1255
01:30:56.992 --> 01:30:59.119
After all, you are the one
who set me free...

1256
01:31:00.412 --> 01:31:01.413
again.

1257
01:31:03.457 --> 01:31:04.542
So, you, more than anyone,

1258
01:31:04.625 --> 01:31:06.252
understands why
I can't go back.

1259
01:31:08.837 --> 01:31:10.631
You should have
listened to me.

1260
01:31:12.841 --> 01:31:14.593
Now you'll never
see her again.

1261
01:31:28.190 --> 01:31:29.358
What was that?

1262
01:31:29.441 --> 01:31:30.818
That was Neo.

1263
01:31:32.444 --> 01:31:33.445
Mojo rising.

1264
01:31:41.495 --> 01:31:42.955
You all right?

1265
01:31:43.038 --> 01:31:44.540
Yeah.

1266
01:31:44.623 --> 01:31:45.791
It's gonna trigger a response.

1267
01:31:45.875 --> 01:31:47.084
I got multiple exits ready.

1268
01:31:47.167 --> 01:31:48.627
This is not over yet!

1269
01:31:48.711 --> 01:31:51.422
Our sequel franchise spinoff!

1270
01:31:58.470 --> 01:31:59.888
We should go.

1271
01:31:59.972 --> 01:32:01.140
I can't.

1272
01:32:01.223 --> 01:32:03.142
I have to talk to her.

1273
01:32:03.225 --> 01:32:05.477
Neo, those Exiles
were older than you,

1274
01:32:05.561 --> 01:32:06.645
and we barely handled them.

1275
01:32:10.232 --> 01:32:11.775
You really wanna do this now?

1276
01:32:17.197 --> 01:32:18.407
I mean...

1277
01:32:22.411 --> 01:32:23.996
you look like shit.

1278
01:32:35.257 --> 01:32:37.801
Oh, my God. What?
What happened?

1279
01:32:37.885 --> 01:32:39.011
An accident.

1280
01:32:39.094 --> 01:32:41.430
Kush! Call a doctor.

1281
01:32:41.513 --> 01:32:43.057
It's fine.

1282
01:32:43.974 --> 01:32:46.101
I don't have a lot of time.

1283
01:32:46.185 --> 01:32:47.895
I wasn't sure
I'd see you again.

1284
01:32:47.978 --> 01:32:50.564
After we spoke, I realized...

1285
01:32:51.440 --> 01:32:53.484
my life wasn't a life.

1286
01:32:54.943 --> 01:32:57.696
At some point,
I think I gave up

1287
01:32:57.780 --> 01:33:00.032
searching for something real.

1288
01:33:06.372 --> 01:33:07.665
Wait.

1289
01:33:09.124 --> 01:33:11.710
Something happened.

1290
01:33:11.794 --> 01:33:14.171
I looked for you
at the coffee shop.

1291
01:33:15.964 --> 01:33:18.300
I began to wonder
if I imagined you.

1292
01:33:19.468 --> 01:33:22.012
And then last night
I had a dream.

1293
01:33:22.096 --> 01:33:24.890
In the dream, you were
surrounded by police,

1294
01:33:24.973 --> 01:33:27.518
then they started chasing us.

1295
01:33:27.601 --> 01:33:30.604
- Us?
- You were on my bike with me.

1296
01:33:32.773 --> 01:33:34.149
How did it end?

1297
01:33:35.567 --> 01:33:36.735
Not good.

1298
01:33:39.279 --> 01:33:42.700
I've had dreams
that weren't just dreams.

1299
01:33:42.783 --> 01:33:45.035
You mean a dream
that came true?

1300
01:33:52.710 --> 01:33:55.337
Finally, we can talk
like adults.

1301
01:33:57.005 --> 01:34:00.134
I hate lying. I do.
It exhausts me.

1302
01:34:01.927 --> 01:34:04.012
Tiff and I have been
waiting for you...

1303
01:34:04.096 --> 01:34:05.347
like, forever.

1304
01:34:12.438 --> 01:34:13.731
Deja vu, right?

1305
01:34:15.524 --> 01:34:17.693
Oh, no use.
You can't beat time.

1306
01:34:17.776 --> 01:34:21.488
This rewind is happening
faster than you can blink.

1307
01:34:26.368 --> 01:34:28.370
You gave me the idea.

1308
01:34:31.206 --> 01:34:34.501
Allow me to sum up our goal
in a single word.

1309
01:34:37.546 --> 01:34:38.672
"Bullet time."

1310
01:34:40.507 --> 01:34:42.468
I know. Kind of ironic,

1311
01:34:42.551 --> 01:34:46.472
using the power that defined
you to control you.

1312
01:34:46.555 --> 01:34:49.183
I kept such a close eye on you

1313
01:34:49.266 --> 01:34:51.810
and still you found a way out.

1314
01:34:51.894 --> 01:34:54.271
Clever monkey,
using that Modal.

1315
01:34:55.230 --> 01:34:56.398
Call me an optimist,

1316
01:34:56.482 --> 01:34:58.650
but this could
all be for the best.

1317
01:34:58.734 --> 01:35:01.570
The skin's not looking
too bad this time.

1318
01:35:01.653 --> 01:35:04.281
I know some of this will be
difficult for you to hear,

1319
01:35:04.364 --> 01:35:05.824
after everything
you went through.

1320
01:35:05.908 --> 01:35:07.284
All that pain and suffering,

1321
01:35:07.367 --> 01:35:10.204
only to learn the world
doesn't end when you do.

1322
01:35:11.747 --> 01:35:12.831
Surprise.

1323
01:35:18.837 --> 01:35:20.255
I was there when you died.

1324
01:35:22.758 --> 01:35:23.884
I said to myself,

1325
01:35:23.967 --> 01:35:27.179
"Here is the anomaly
of anomalies."

1326
01:35:27.262 --> 01:35:30.057
What an extraordinary
opportunity.

1327
01:35:31.725 --> 01:35:33.185
First, I had to convince
the Suits

1328
01:35:33.268 --> 01:35:34.686
to let me rebuild
the two of you.

1329
01:35:34.770 --> 01:35:36.355
Why her? Getting there.

1330
01:35:36.438 --> 01:35:38.232
And don't worry,
she can't hear me.

1331
01:35:38.315 --> 01:35:41.443
Resurrecting you both
was crazy expensive.

1332
01:35:41.527 --> 01:35:42.861
Like renovating a house.

1333
01:35:42.945 --> 01:35:45.197
Took twice as long,
cost twice as much.

1334
01:35:49.284 --> 01:35:51.745
I thought you'd be happy
to be alive again.

1335
01:35:52.788 --> 01:35:54.039
So wrong.

1336
01:35:55.833 --> 01:35:59.461
Did you know hope and despair
are nearly identical in code?

1337
01:36:01.463 --> 01:36:03.423
We worked for years,

1338
01:36:03.507 --> 01:36:05.134
<i>trying to activate
your source code.</i>

1339
01:36:05.217 --> 01:36:08.637
I was about to give up,
when I realized...

1340
01:36:11.723 --> 01:36:12.766
Trinity.

1341
01:36:12.850 --> 01:36:15.018
...it was never just you.

1342
01:36:15.102 --> 01:36:18.188
Alone, neither of you
is of any particular value.

1343
01:36:19.898 --> 01:36:21.066
Like acids and bases,

1344
01:36:21.149 --> 01:36:23.527
you're dangerous
when mixed together.

1345
01:36:23.610 --> 01:36:26.572
Every sim
where you two bonded...

1346
01:36:26.655 --> 01:36:28.740
Let's just say
bad things happened.

1347
01:36:30.784 --> 01:36:32.244
Neo!

1348
01:36:36.498 --> 01:36:39.877
However, as long as I managed
to keep you close,

1349
01:36:39.960 --> 01:36:41.628
but not too close,

1350
01:36:41.712 --> 01:36:44.923
I discovered
something incredible.

1351
01:36:45.007 --> 01:36:48.510
Now, my predecessor
loved precision.

1352
01:36:48.594 --> 01:36:52.264
His Matrix was all fussy facts
and equations.

1353
01:36:52.347 --> 01:36:54.099
He hated the human mind.

1354
01:36:54.182 --> 01:36:55.601
So he never bothered
to realize

1355
01:36:55.684 --> 01:36:56.852
that you don't give a shit
about facts.

1356
01:36:56.935 --> 01:36:58.353
It's all about fiction.

1357
01:36:58.437 --> 01:37:03.108
The only world that matters
is the one in here.

1358
01:37:03.192 --> 01:37:06.194
And you people
believe the craziest shit.

1359
01:37:06.737 --> 01:37:07.988
Why?

1360
01:37:08.071 --> 01:37:10.657
What validates
and makes your fictions real?

1361
01:37:11.617 --> 01:37:12.701
Feelings.

1362
01:37:13.869 --> 01:37:15.329
Allow me.

1363
01:37:16.705 --> 01:37:18.373
Kush, here,
is one of my handlers.

1364
01:37:18.457 --> 01:37:19.791
They're everywhere.

1365
01:37:19.875 --> 01:37:22.461
Such a pain, cloning Agents
over a coppertop.

1366
01:37:22.544 --> 01:37:25.005
Far more effective
just to saturate a population.

1367
01:37:26.924 --> 01:37:29.801
And, bonus,
swarm mode is sick fun.

1368
01:37:42.230 --> 01:37:45.359
Ooh! Nicely done.

1369
01:37:46.818 --> 01:37:50.072
You ever wonder
why you have nightmares?

1370
01:37:50.155 --> 01:37:53.116
Why your own brain
tortures you?

1371
01:37:53.200 --> 01:37:56.703
It's actually us,
maximizing your output.

1372
01:37:56.787 --> 01:37:57.955
It works just like this.

1373
01:37:58.038 --> 01:38:00.666
Oh, no!
Can you stop the bullet?

1374
01:38:00.749 --> 01:38:03.669
If only you could move faster.

1375
01:38:03.752 --> 01:38:06.296
Here's the thing
about feelings.

1376
01:38:06.380 --> 01:38:08.674
They're so much easier
to control than facts.

1377
01:38:09.633 --> 01:38:11.510
Turns out, in my Matrix,

1378
01:38:11.593 --> 01:38:15.055
the worse we treat you,
the more we manipulate you,

1379
01:38:15.138 --> 01:38:17.599
the more energy you produce.

1380
01:38:17.683 --> 01:38:19.893
It's nuts.

1381
01:38:19.977 --> 01:38:21.561
I've been setting
productivity records

1382
01:38:21.645 --> 01:38:22.938
every year since I took over.

1383
01:38:23.021 --> 01:38:25.857
And, the best part,
zero resistance.

1384
01:38:25.941 --> 01:38:27.317
People stay in their pods,

1385
01:38:27.401 --> 01:38:30.487
happier than pigs in shit.

1386
01:38:30.570 --> 01:38:31.780
The key to it all?

1387
01:38:31.863 --> 01:38:33.198
You.

1388
01:38:33.281 --> 01:38:34.449
And her.

1389
01:38:34.533 --> 01:38:36.743
Quietly yearning
for what you don't have,

1390
01:38:36.827 --> 01:38:39.246
while dreading
losing what you do.

1391
01:38:39.329 --> 01:38:40.998
For 99.9% of your race,

1392
01:38:41.081 --> 01:38:43.750
that is the definition
of reality.

1393
01:38:43.834 --> 01:38:46.712
Desire and fear, baby.

1394
01:38:46.795 --> 01:38:49.756
Just give the people
what they want, right?

1395
01:38:59.057 --> 01:39:02.102
She's the only home
you have, Thomas.

1396
01:39:02.185 --> 01:39:05.480
Come home before
something terrible happens.

1397
01:39:15.907 --> 01:39:17.200
- Bugs!
- I hear him.

1398
01:39:23.582 --> 01:39:24.750
Trinity!

1399
01:39:24.833 --> 01:39:26.543
- You shouldn't call me that.
- I'm sorry.

1400
01:39:28.045 --> 01:39:29.296
I have to go.

1401
01:39:29.379 --> 01:39:30.547
But I'll be back.

1402
01:39:31.673 --> 01:39:33.967
Neo! Time to go.

1403
01:39:36.470 --> 01:39:38.180
- Sentinels?
- Worse.

1404
01:39:39.639 --> 01:39:40.724
<i>General ordered me</i>

1405
01:39:40.807 --> 01:39:41.808
<i>to look after the ship.</i>

1406
01:39:41.892 --> 01:39:43.769
So you shadowed us?

1407
01:39:43.852 --> 01:39:45.437
Check your long-range scans.

1408
01:39:45.520 --> 01:39:47.522
<i>Squids are combing this area.</i>

1409
01:39:47.606 --> 01:39:49.066
He's right.

1410
01:39:49.149 --> 01:39:50.317
You can stay here and die,

1411
01:39:50.400 --> 01:39:52.778
or come back
and face a court-martial.

1412
01:39:52.861 --> 01:39:54.863
And you call that a choice?

1413
01:40:02.079 --> 01:40:04.206
Sheperd should have
left you to the Squids.

1414
01:40:04.289 --> 01:40:07.667
I'm too damn old to sit
through some boring-ass trial.

1415
01:40:07.751 --> 01:40:08.960
Niobe, don't blame Bugs.

1416
01:40:09.044 --> 01:40:10.962
Do shut your mouth.

1417
01:40:11.046 --> 01:40:13.340
Do address me as General.

1418
01:40:13.423 --> 01:40:17.677
And do not rob
my ex-captain of her agency,

1419
01:40:17.761 --> 01:40:19.763
which she exercised
with her own

1420
01:40:19.846 --> 01:40:23.350
particular brand
of shortsighted stupidity.

1421
01:40:24.601 --> 01:40:25.685
Shortsighted?

1422
01:40:27.354 --> 01:40:31.316
You care more about growing
fruit than freeing minds.

1423
01:40:31.399 --> 01:40:33.902
We are not going
to have this argument again.

1424
01:40:33.985 --> 01:40:36.321
It's not an argument.
It's a fact.

1425
01:40:36.404 --> 01:40:37.614
You gave up on people.

1426
01:40:39.074 --> 01:40:41.409
I tell you
what I'm going to give up on

1427
01:40:41.493 --> 01:40:42.577
and it's you!

1428
01:40:44.996 --> 01:40:46.915
Sheperd, get her
out of my sight!

1429
01:40:46.998 --> 01:40:48.125
General...

1430
01:40:50.043 --> 01:40:51.128
Disarm!

1431
01:40:51.211 --> 01:40:52.838
Kujaku's a friend.

1432
01:40:59.386 --> 01:41:01.012
Hello, friend.

1433
01:41:03.598 --> 01:41:04.599
Okay.

1434
01:41:05.934 --> 01:41:07.144
Him?

1435
01:41:14.067 --> 01:41:15.735
General.

1436
01:41:15.819 --> 01:41:17.112
Thank you for seeing me.

1437
01:41:17.195 --> 01:41:18.989
I figured if there was anyone

1438
01:41:19.072 --> 01:41:21.366
who could make sense
of this mess,

1439
01:41:21.449 --> 01:41:23.243
it would be you.

1440
01:41:23.326 --> 01:41:24.452
Hello, Neo.

1441
01:41:24.536 --> 01:41:26.371
I know you.

1442
01:41:26.454 --> 01:41:28.456
I tried to keep my eye on you.

1443
01:41:31.793 --> 01:41:33.044
Why?

1444
01:41:33.128 --> 01:41:34.880
We met a long time ago.

1445
01:41:36.590 --> 01:41:37.674
Good morning.

1446
01:41:40.468 --> 01:41:41.469
Sati.

1447
01:41:41.553 --> 01:41:44.055
My father knew
we'd meet again,

1448
01:41:44.139 --> 01:41:47.100
though he would have wished
for happier circumstances.

1449
01:41:47.184 --> 01:41:48.977
His inadvertent role
in what happened to you

1450
01:41:49.060 --> 01:41:51.313
was the greatest regret
of his life.

1451
01:41:51.396 --> 01:41:53.273
I don't understand.

1452
01:41:54.649 --> 01:41:56.318
My father
was the chief engineer

1453
01:41:56.401 --> 01:41:57.652
at the Anomaleum.

1454
01:41:57.736 --> 01:41:59.112
The what?

1455
01:41:59.196 --> 01:42:02.282
My father designed
the resurrection pods

1456
01:42:02.365 --> 01:42:04.284
where Neo and Trinity
were imprisoned.

1457
01:42:06.328 --> 01:42:07.579
I'm sorry.

1458
01:42:07.662 --> 01:42:09.164
You knew what happened to him?

1459
01:42:09.247 --> 01:42:12.459
You knew that he and Trinity
both were alive...

1460
01:42:13.460 --> 01:42:14.753
and you didn't tell me?

1461
01:42:14.836 --> 01:42:17.756
There were times
I doubted my decision, Niobe.

1462
01:42:17.839 --> 01:42:19.466
But Io needed you.

1463
01:42:19.549 --> 01:42:20.884
This city needed to be built

1464
01:42:20.967 --> 01:42:23.011
for your people
as well as mine.

1465
01:42:24.179 --> 01:42:25.931
If I would have
told you everything,

1466
01:42:26.014 --> 01:42:28.183
you would have had a very
difficult choice to make.

1467
01:42:28.266 --> 01:42:29.851
My friends

1468
01:42:31.186 --> 01:42:33.688
let me make my own choices.

1469
01:42:33.772 --> 01:42:35.690
If it was a mistake,

1470
01:42:35.774 --> 01:42:37.859
you have my deepest apologies.

1471
01:42:39.945 --> 01:42:41.279
Why are you here now?

1472
01:42:41.363 --> 01:42:43.865
Neo's escape has
destabilized the Matrix.

1473
01:42:43.949 --> 01:42:45.200
The Anomaleum
draws its current

1474
01:42:45.283 --> 01:42:46.618
from Trinity alone now.

1475
01:42:46.701 --> 01:42:48.870
A fail-safe has been
triggered to reset

1476
01:42:48.954 --> 01:42:50.956
the Matrix back
to the previous version.

1477
01:42:51.039 --> 01:42:52.832
But The Analyst
halted the reset.

1478
01:42:52.916 --> 01:42:54.209
He's convinced the authorities

1479
01:42:54.292 --> 01:42:56.253
that you will soon
return voluntarily.

1480
01:42:57.379 --> 01:42:59.297
And why would he say that?

1481
01:42:59.381 --> 01:43:02.467
Because if I don't go back,
he'll kill Trinity.

1482
01:43:05.220 --> 01:43:07.597
Faced with returning
to your pod

1483
01:43:07.681 --> 01:43:10.475
or enduring
Trinity's death again.

1484
01:43:10.558 --> 01:43:11.851
What would you choose, Neo?

1485
01:43:12.936 --> 01:43:14.229
I'll go back.

1486
01:43:15.939 --> 01:43:18.149
Well, The Analyst
knows you well,

1487
01:43:18.233 --> 01:43:20.986
but that knowledge
has made him incautious.

1488
01:43:21.069 --> 01:43:22.737
After you escaped,

1489
01:43:22.821 --> 01:43:25.657
he should have accepted his
losses and devacuated Trinity.

1490
01:43:25.740 --> 01:43:28.618
But that would have prevented
this extraordinary opportunity

1491
01:43:28.702 --> 01:43:30.620
that now exists before us.

1492
01:43:31.288 --> 01:43:34.207
A few hours ago,

1493
01:43:34.291 --> 01:43:37.585
no one would have been able
to convince me

1494
01:43:37.669 --> 01:43:41.965
that I would be standing here,
trying to explain a mission

1495
01:43:42.048 --> 01:43:44.009
as crazy as this one.

1496
01:43:47.804 --> 01:43:49.431
What are you doing?

1497
01:43:49.514 --> 01:43:51.057
- Volunteering.
- Oh, no.

1498
01:43:51.141 --> 01:43:55.687
You are the one captain
that I am ordering to go.

1499
01:43:55.770 --> 01:43:57.355
Now you don't
have to order me, General,

1500
01:43:57.439 --> 01:43:59.107
'cause I'm volunteering.

1501
01:44:02.485 --> 01:44:04.029
I need two more.

1502
01:44:08.533 --> 01:44:11.369
Are you out of your minds?

1503
01:44:11.453 --> 01:44:13.330
You don't even know
what it is.

1504
01:44:13.413 --> 01:44:16.333
General, we know you.

1505
01:44:16.416 --> 01:44:17.625
If you say this is important,

1506
01:44:17.709 --> 01:44:19.753
none of us is
choosing to stay home.

1507
01:44:25.133 --> 01:44:26.217
Thank you.

1508
01:44:31.306 --> 01:44:33.308
Knuckle up, and good luck.

1509
01:45:03.338 --> 01:45:04.839
Trinity is held
in the Anomaleum,

1510
01:45:04.923 --> 01:45:06.674
which is in this
transmission tower.

1511
01:45:06.758 --> 01:45:09.010
<i>The passages used
to rescue Neo are now sealed</i>

1512
01:45:09.094 --> 01:45:11.304
<i>and a legion of Sentinels
patrols the tower.</i>

1513
01:45:11.388 --> 01:45:13.431
So, stealth will be paramount.

1514
01:45:13.515 --> 01:45:15.266
As long as we raise no alarms,

1515
01:45:15.350 --> 01:45:17.435
this first part of the mission
should be the easiest.

1516
01:45:17.519 --> 01:45:18.770
You mean
crossing the Fetus Fields,

1517
01:45:18.853 --> 01:45:20.605
sneaking across
an entire power plant,

1518
01:45:20.688 --> 01:45:22.107
climbing
a two-kilometer tower

1519
01:45:22.190 --> 01:45:24.025
guarded by thousands
of Sentinels?

1520
01:45:24.109 --> 01:45:25.276
That's the easy part?

1521
01:45:25.360 --> 01:45:27.028
Exactly so.

1522
01:45:27.112 --> 01:45:29.447
Because all we have to do
is convince someone

1523
01:45:29.531 --> 01:45:31.199
who does this every day

1524
01:45:31.282 --> 01:45:32.700
to take one of us along.

1525
01:45:56.224 --> 01:45:58.059
Fifty meters
below the Anomaleum

1526
01:45:58.143 --> 01:45:59.644
is a stratum
of amniotic filters.

1527
01:45:59.727 --> 01:46:03.148
Hidden along this edge
is a small hexagonal vent.

1528
01:46:03.231 --> 01:46:06.401
<i>This vent feeds the air intake
into the corpuscular modifier,</i>

1529
01:46:06.484 --> 01:46:09.571
<i>which oxygenates
the bio-gel used in Neo's pod.</i>

1530
01:46:10.238 --> 01:46:11.448
I get it.

1531
01:46:11.531 --> 01:46:14.409
The exomorph slinkies up
Neo's old umbilicus.

1532
01:46:15.660 --> 01:46:16.786
What could go wrong?

1533
01:47:03.666 --> 01:47:05.043
<i>Once inside,</i>

1534
01:47:05.126 --> 01:47:06.961
<i>Morpheus will use
the System Operator</i>

1535
01:47:07.045 --> 01:47:09.380
<i>to open the devacuator line
and disengage the macerators.</i>

1536
01:47:13.468 --> 01:47:15.053
In order to unplug
Trinity's body,

1537
01:47:15.136 --> 01:47:17.347
while her mind still remains
connected to the Matrix,

1538
01:47:17.430 --> 01:47:19.057
I'm gonna need
a second human brain

1539
01:47:19.140 --> 01:47:20.350
to implement the bypass.

1540
01:47:20.433 --> 01:47:22.060
And since Neo
must be with The Analyst,

1541
01:47:22.143 --> 01:47:25.313
the only available mind
that's a near-enough match

1542
01:47:25.396 --> 01:47:26.439
is yours.

1543
01:47:27.982 --> 01:47:28.900
Figures.

1544
01:47:46.417 --> 01:47:47.544
Thanks, Cybebe.

1545
01:47:55.760 --> 01:47:57.762
Does Trinity still have
to take the red pill?

1546
01:47:57.845 --> 01:47:59.264
Since Kujaku and I
are transferring

1547
01:47:59.347 --> 01:48:00.640
her consciousness
onto the ship,

1548
01:48:00.723 --> 01:48:02.392
it's not strictly necessary.

1549
01:48:02.475 --> 01:48:06.396
But what matters is that
this is her choice.

1550
01:48:06.479 --> 01:48:09.774
Extracting a confused
or an uncertain mind will,

1551
01:48:09.857 --> 01:48:11.234
in all probability, kill her.

1552
01:48:11.317 --> 01:48:13.861
But even if it is
what she wants,

1553
01:48:13.945 --> 01:48:17.615
won't The Analyst just order
the Sentinels to stop you?

1554
01:48:17.699 --> 01:48:19.200
He will.

1555
01:48:19.284 --> 01:48:21.744
But if my plan works,
it won't matter.

1556
01:48:21.828 --> 01:48:22.787
Why?

1557
01:48:22.870 --> 01:48:24.497
Because we'll already be gone.

1558
01:48:26.207 --> 01:48:28.126
Somebody thinks
this hard about a plan,

1559
01:48:28.209 --> 01:48:29.627
there has to be a reason why.

1560
01:48:31.838 --> 01:48:33.047
When my father realized

1561
01:48:33.131 --> 01:48:35.383
how the Anomaleum
was going to be used,

1562
01:48:35.466 --> 01:48:38.928
he covertly transferred
the designs to me.

1563
01:48:39.012 --> 01:48:41.514
The Analyst
discovered his betrayal

1564
01:48:41.598 --> 01:48:43.474
and had my parents purged.

1565
01:48:46.102 --> 01:48:49.105
I would have been murdered too
if it wasn't for Kujaku.

1566
01:48:52.150 --> 01:48:56.154
Not a day goes by
that I don't grieve them.

1567
01:48:56.237 --> 01:48:59.365
I've been praying for this day
for a very long time.

1568
01:49:07.457 --> 01:49:09.000
We're coming up on broadcast.

1569
01:49:11.586 --> 01:49:15.590
I thought you should know
that I'm here because of her.

1570
01:49:19.093 --> 01:49:21.471
All I ever wanted was to be
as fearless as Trinity.

1571
01:49:23.681 --> 01:49:27.101
But I saw how she reacted
in the garage, and I...

1572
01:49:27.185 --> 01:49:29.812
You're wondering if I'm wrong.

1573
01:49:29.896 --> 01:49:31.439
What if we're too late?

1574
01:49:33.232 --> 01:49:34.942
What if she's not
Trinity anymore?

1575
01:49:40.365 --> 01:49:43.117
I never believed
I was The One.

1576
01:49:43.993 --> 01:49:45.411
But she did.

1577
01:49:46.454 --> 01:49:48.081
She believed in me.

1578
01:49:50.750 --> 01:49:52.960
It's my turn
to believe in her.

1579
01:50:17.944 --> 01:50:19.862
This is
where it gets tricky.

1580
01:50:30.998 --> 01:50:33.418
Have you ever done
an operation like this?

1581
01:50:34.127 --> 01:50:35.211
Not yet.

1582
01:50:56.941 --> 01:50:58.276
Here we go.

1583
01:51:15.918 --> 01:51:17.837
Welcome home.

1584
01:51:17.920 --> 01:51:20.298
All I want is to talk to her.

1585
01:51:20.381 --> 01:51:22.008
Do you mean Tiff?

1586
01:51:22.091 --> 01:51:24.844
Come back, and you can talk
to her as often as you like.

1587
01:51:24.927 --> 01:51:26.304
I mean, handsome Chad

1588
01:51:26.387 --> 01:51:27.847
may have something
to say about it.

1589
01:51:27.930 --> 01:51:31.225
If she tells me
this is what she wants,

1590
01:51:32.435 --> 01:51:33.603
you win.

1591
01:51:33.686 --> 01:51:34.812
Really?

1592
01:51:34.896 --> 01:51:37.648
But if she wants me,

1593
01:51:37.732 --> 01:51:39.567
then you'll let us go free.

1594
01:51:39.650 --> 01:51:42.403
And why would I do something
as stupid as that?

1595
01:51:42.487 --> 01:51:45.281
Right now, I'm on a ship full
of people who will unplug me

1596
01:51:45.364 --> 01:51:48.367
before they'll let you
take me back.

1597
01:51:48.451 --> 01:51:50.495
If you want this Matrix,

1598
01:51:50.578 --> 01:51:52.121
this is your only chance.

1599
01:51:52.205 --> 01:51:55.166
But how do I know
they won't unplug you anyway?

1600
01:51:55.249 --> 01:51:58.586
Same way I know you'll let us
walk out of here.

1601
01:52:24.195 --> 01:52:25.863
Okay.

1602
01:52:25.947 --> 01:52:27.448
I like tests.

1603
01:52:28.324 --> 01:52:30.117
We'll let Tiff decide.

1604
01:52:47.468 --> 01:52:48.636
That's it.

1605
01:52:49.846 --> 01:52:51.389
Bypass is ready.

1606
01:52:51.472 --> 01:52:53.182
Now what?

1607
01:52:53.266 --> 01:52:54.517
We wait.

1608
01:52:54.600 --> 01:52:56.561
Doesn't it seem crazy
to come all this way

1609
01:52:56.644 --> 01:52:58.229
and leave her here?

1610
01:52:58.312 --> 01:53:00.982
We must abide by her decision.

1611
01:53:01.065 --> 01:53:02.650
And if she says no,

1612
01:53:03.484 --> 01:53:04.944
what happens to Neo?

1613
01:53:05.027 --> 01:53:06.237
At this time,

1614
01:53:06.320 --> 01:53:09.156
the most important choice
of Neo's life

1615
01:53:09.240 --> 01:53:10.741
is not his to make.

1616
01:53:41.772 --> 01:53:43.566
I saw this in my dream.

1617
01:53:45.026 --> 01:53:48.487
If I was the Oracle,
maybe I could explain it.

1618
01:53:49.155 --> 01:53:50.740
The Oracle.

1619
01:53:50.823 --> 01:53:52.491
From your game?

1620
01:53:54.368 --> 01:53:56.621
It's not a game.

1621
01:53:58.748 --> 01:53:59.957
Oh, God.

1622
01:54:07.423 --> 01:54:10.843
After you left, I went home

1623
01:54:10.927 --> 01:54:12.637
and I played it.

1624
01:54:15.014 --> 01:54:17.475
I kept thinking,

1625
01:54:17.558 --> 01:54:20.895
why does this story
feel like a memory?

1626
01:54:28.069 --> 01:54:29.820
There's a part of me

1627
01:54:32.406 --> 01:54:35.618
that feels like I have been
waiting my whole life for you.

1628
01:54:38.579 --> 01:54:40.831
And that part is like,

1629
01:54:40.915 --> 01:54:44.627
"What the hell
took you so long?"

1630
01:54:44.710 --> 01:54:46.754
I don't have an easy answer.

1631
01:54:48.923 --> 01:54:51.092
Maybe I was afraid of this.

1632
01:54:52.551 --> 01:54:54.428
Afraid of what might happen.

1633
01:54:55.930 --> 01:54:58.933
Afraid of hurting
the only person I ever loved.

1634
01:55:00.643 --> 01:55:04.188
I wish I was
who you think I am.

1635
01:55:05.564 --> 01:55:07.149
But look at me.

1636
01:55:08.442 --> 01:55:10.611
I can't be her.

1637
01:55:10.695 --> 01:55:12.822
- Mom!
- Mom! Come on.

1638
01:55:12.905 --> 01:55:14.156
- Mom!
- It's Callie.

1639
01:55:14.240 --> 01:55:15.241
Is this real?

1640
01:55:15.324 --> 01:55:16.492
You have to come with us.

1641
01:55:16.575 --> 01:55:17.952
Come on,
we gotta go.

1642
01:55:18.035 --> 01:55:19.537
Tiff, hey. Don't know
what's going on here,

1643
01:55:19.620 --> 01:55:20.955
but I'm glad we found you.

1644
01:55:21.038 --> 01:55:22.331
- She got hit by a car!
- I know, it's crazy.

1645
01:55:22.415 --> 01:55:23.541
She was chasing after you.

1646
01:55:23.624 --> 01:55:24.959
They're casting her arm.
We gotta go.

1647
01:55:25.042 --> 01:55:26.419
Doctor said
she's gonna be fine.

1648
01:55:26.502 --> 01:55:28.295
You have to come
with us to the hospital.

1649
01:55:28.379 --> 01:55:29.463
It's too late.

1650
01:55:29.547 --> 01:55:30.756
I understand.

1651
01:55:30.840 --> 01:55:32.675
- Tiff, come on, let's go.
- Come on.

1652
01:55:39.181 --> 01:55:40.266
What's happening?

1653
01:55:42.351 --> 01:55:43.477
Neo was wrong.

1654
01:56:16.844 --> 01:56:17.928
Tiffany.

1655
01:56:21.515 --> 01:56:24.060
Tiffany, you have
to come with us.

1656
01:56:25.686 --> 01:56:27.063
Tiffany!

1657
01:56:29.356 --> 01:56:33.069
I wish you would
fucking stop calling me that.

1658
01:56:33.152 --> 01:56:34.695
I hate that name.

1659
01:56:36.197 --> 01:56:37.740
My name is Trinity

1660
01:56:37.823 --> 01:56:40.201
and you better
take your hands off of me.

1661
01:56:51.378 --> 01:56:52.379
Neo!

1662
01:56:52.880 --> 01:56:53.881
Trinity!

1663
01:56:55.049 --> 01:56:56.092
Oh, shit.

1664
01:56:57.384 --> 01:56:58.719
Get her out. Get her out!

1665
01:57:07.353 --> 01:57:10.648
Aye-yi-yi, what a mess.

1666
01:57:10.731 --> 01:57:13.400
I own that mistake.
Shouldn't have pressed.

1667
01:57:13.484 --> 01:57:16.487
Women used to be
so easy to control.

1668
01:57:16.570 --> 01:57:21.117
You know there's no way
I can let you two go free.

1669
01:57:24.537 --> 01:57:25.996
Cannot happen.

1670
01:57:29.166 --> 01:57:32.002
So, I guess it's deja vu
all over again.

1671
01:57:33.129 --> 01:57:34.922
She dies

1672
01:57:35.005 --> 01:57:36.382
and it's all your fault.

1673
01:57:37.925 --> 01:57:40.511
Lies, lies and more lies.

1674
01:57:41.262 --> 01:57:42.471
Smith?

1675
01:57:42.555 --> 01:57:43.681
What has the world come to

1676
01:57:43.764 --> 01:57:44.932
when you can't even
trust a program?

1677
01:57:45.015 --> 01:57:48.352
How...

1678
01:57:48.435 --> 01:57:51.188
Tom and I have more in common
than you know.

1679
01:57:51.272 --> 01:57:54.316
Once he got out,
let's just say,

1680
01:57:55.151 --> 01:57:56.944
I was free to be me.

1681
01:58:04.618 --> 01:58:07.371
- Yeah!
- Trinity?

1682
01:58:55.753 --> 01:58:56.921
You ready?

1683
01:58:57.004 --> 01:58:58.297
Yeah.

1684
01:59:40.381 --> 01:59:41.840
Oh, no.

1685
01:59:43.217 --> 01:59:45.594
Destroy her. Destroy her!

1686
02:00:02.569 --> 02:00:03.570
No.

1687
02:00:09.410 --> 02:00:10.911
Stop them.

1688
02:00:36.562 --> 02:00:38.063
You think this is over?

1689
02:00:38.147 --> 02:00:40.149
Lockdown. Initiate swarm.

1690
02:00:49.116 --> 02:00:51.452
Here, our unexpected
alliance ends.

1691
02:00:53.120 --> 02:00:55.748
You know the difference
between us, Tom?

1692
02:00:55.831 --> 02:00:57.708
Anyone could have been you.

1693
02:00:57.791 --> 02:00:59.835
Whereas I've always
been anyone.

1694
02:01:05.215 --> 02:01:06.717
What just happened?

1695
02:01:06.800 --> 02:01:07.968
What?

1696
02:01:09.970 --> 02:01:12.556
Oh, no! Move! Move!

1697
02:01:12.639 --> 02:01:13.682
Get the hell out of there!

1698
02:01:17.561 --> 02:01:19.521
- How bad?
- Like, all the bad.

1699
02:01:20.814 --> 02:01:22.274
Yeah, this is bad.

1700
02:01:23.650 --> 02:01:25.277
I don't suppose
you can still fly?

1701
02:01:35.662 --> 02:01:37.373
Yeah, that's not happening.

1702
02:02:03.107 --> 02:02:04.358
Neo! Get on.

1703
02:02:13.033 --> 02:02:14.827
Calliope! Take the wounded!

1704
02:02:14.910 --> 02:02:16.954
Everyone else,
we stay with them!

1705
02:02:34.012 --> 02:02:36.557
- How is she?
- Life signs are good.

1706
02:02:40.394 --> 02:02:41.854
Her signal's strong, Captain.

1707
02:02:50.737 --> 02:02:52.781
Well done, Captain.

1708
02:02:55.159 --> 02:02:57.035
All we need is a miracle.

1709
02:03:25.105 --> 02:03:26.148
I hate bots.

1710
02:03:32.446 --> 02:03:34.281
- Get us out of here!
- I'm trying!

1711
02:03:34.364 --> 02:03:36.366
The lockdown is tracking.
Swarm is everywhere.

1712
02:03:36.450 --> 02:03:37.618
Never seen anything like this.

1713
02:04:23.497 --> 02:04:25.666
Seq, what is that?

1714
02:04:30.671 --> 02:04:31.797
What's wrong?

1715
02:04:33.507 --> 02:04:35.008
What are you...

1716
02:04:42.558 --> 02:04:44.601
He's turning bots into bombs.

1717
02:05:17.050 --> 02:05:18.260
Shit!

1718
02:05:18.343 --> 02:05:19.344
Lexy?

1719
02:05:33.734 --> 02:05:34.943
Sheperd's in trouble.

1720
02:05:38.030 --> 02:05:39.823
Jack me in.

1721
02:05:39.906 --> 02:05:41.950
I can get you in.
I don't know if I can get you out.

1722
02:05:47.914 --> 02:05:49.625
No!

1723
02:06:02.971 --> 02:06:04.097
What are they doing?

1724
02:06:08.143 --> 02:06:09.811
Herding them into a kill zone.

1725
02:06:42.886 --> 02:06:44.221
Captain, you gotta hurry.

1726
02:06:44.304 --> 02:06:46.556
Hang on, Lex.

1727
02:06:50.769 --> 02:06:52.604
Lexy!

1728
02:07:34.855 --> 02:07:36.022
There they are!

1729
02:08:02.466 --> 02:08:03.633
Morpheus!

1730
02:08:07.512 --> 02:08:09.222
Lex.

1731
02:08:09.306 --> 02:08:11.183
- Bugsy.
- Hell yeah!

1732
02:08:12.142 --> 02:08:13.769
Seq, where's Neo?

1733
02:08:13.852 --> 02:08:15.479
It's bad. They're pinned.

1734
02:08:15.562 --> 02:08:16.646
Heading to a roof.

1735
02:09:25.924 --> 02:09:27.175
Nodal fibrillation
is critical.

1736
02:09:27.259 --> 02:09:28.677
She'll die
if we don't extract.

1737
02:10:09.676 --> 02:10:12.304
It's so beautiful.

1738
02:10:27.611 --> 02:10:29.321
I remember this.

1739
02:10:31.406 --> 02:10:33.617
I remember us.

1740
02:10:51.718 --> 02:10:53.720
My dream ended here.

1741
02:11:04.606 --> 02:11:06.191
We can't go back.

1742
02:11:08.318 --> 02:11:09.402
We won't.

1743
02:11:28.672 --> 02:11:30.048
Can they make the jump?

1744
02:12:01.121 --> 02:12:02.747
I'm not doing this.

1745
02:12:02.831 --> 02:12:04.207
Are you doing this?

1746
02:12:28.314 --> 02:12:29.399
Bye.

1747
02:13:50.438 --> 02:13:52.023
How dramatic.

1748
02:13:52.857 --> 02:13:54.150
"Tiffany"?

1749
02:13:54.234 --> 02:13:57.195
It was a private joke.

1750
02:13:57.278 --> 02:13:58.822
An amusement, that's all.

1751
02:13:58.905 --> 02:14:01.241
An amusement? Hmm.

1752
02:14:02.992 --> 02:14:05.161
Whoa.

1753
02:14:05.245 --> 02:14:06.663
Kind of like that?

1754
02:14:10.917 --> 02:14:13.670
Okay. Ow.

1755
02:14:13.753 --> 02:14:15.213
If you hated the name so much,

1756
02:14:15.296 --> 02:14:17.465
why did you heel like
a good little bitch so long?

1757
02:14:20.593 --> 02:14:22.846
Yeah. Definitely asked
for that.

1758
02:14:28.143 --> 02:14:30.103
Can't you control her?

1759
02:14:35.942 --> 02:14:37.652
That was for using children.

1760
02:14:42.532 --> 02:14:44.033
We have a few questions.

1761
02:14:44.117 --> 02:14:45.952
You tried to activate
the fail-safe.

1762
02:14:46.035 --> 02:14:47.370
The Suits tried.

1763
02:14:47.453 --> 02:14:49.747
Obviously, without control
of your source code,

1764
02:14:49.831 --> 02:14:51.207
I knew that was impossible.

1765
02:14:51.291 --> 02:14:53.501
So, why haven't
the Suits purged you?

1766
02:14:54.377 --> 02:14:57.046
Because I know the system.

1767
02:14:57.130 --> 02:14:59.549
I know human beings.

1768
02:14:59.632 --> 02:15:01.801
And I know you.

1769
02:15:04.220 --> 02:15:06.764
Right now, you're feeling good
about what you've done.

1770
02:15:06.848 --> 02:15:09.267
You should.
It was a victory. Bravo.

1771
02:15:10.101 --> 02:15:11.436
Now what?

1772
02:15:11.519 --> 02:15:14.147
You've come here to negotiate
some kind of deal?

1773
02:15:14.230 --> 02:15:15.815
You think you hold
all the cards,

1774
02:15:15.899 --> 02:15:18.318
because you can do whatever
you want in this world.

1775
02:15:18.401 --> 02:15:20.737
I say, go for it.

1776
02:15:20.820 --> 02:15:23.406
Remake it.
Knock yourselves out.

1777
02:15:23.489 --> 02:15:25.533
Paint the sky with rainbows.

1778
02:15:25.617 --> 02:15:26.784
But here's the thing.

1779
02:15:26.868 --> 02:15:29.913
The sheeple aren't
going anywhere.

1780
02:15:29.996 --> 02:15:31.206
They like my world.

1781
02:15:31.289 --> 02:15:34.209
They don't want
this sentimentality.

1782
02:15:34.292 --> 02:15:36.211
They don't want
freedom or empowerment.

1783
02:15:36.294 --> 02:15:38.713
They want to be controlled.

1784
02:15:38.796 --> 02:15:40.757
They crave
the comfort of certainty.

1785
02:15:40.840 --> 02:15:43.593
And that means you two,
back in your pods,

1786
02:15:43.676 --> 02:15:47.222
unconscious and alone,
just like them.

1787
02:15:51.476 --> 02:15:54.187
We're not here
to negotiate anything.

1788
02:15:54.270 --> 02:15:56.522
We were on our way
to remake your world.

1789
02:15:56.606 --> 02:15:58.149
Change a few things.

1790
02:15:58.233 --> 02:15:59.442
I kind of like

1791
02:15:59.525 --> 02:16:00.860
the "paint the sky
with rainbows" idea.

1792
02:16:00.944 --> 02:16:02.862
Just remind people
what a free mind can do.

1793
02:16:02.946 --> 02:16:04.447
I forgot. It's easy to forget.

1794
02:16:04.530 --> 02:16:06.950
- He makes it easy.
- That, he does.

1795
02:16:07.033 --> 02:16:09.244
Something he should
think about.

1796
02:16:10.245 --> 02:16:11.454
Before we got started,

1797
02:16:11.537 --> 02:16:14.374
we decided to stop by
to say thank you.

1798
02:16:14.457 --> 02:16:17.543
You gave us something
we never thought we could have.

1799
02:16:17.627 --> 02:16:19.003
And what is that?

1800
02:16:19.879 --> 02:16:21.673
Another chance.

1801
02:27:24.919 --> 02:27:27.713
Face reality, people.
Movies are dead.

1802
02:27:27.796 --> 02:27:29.715
Games are dead.

1803
02:27:29.798 --> 02:27:31.550
Narrative? Dead.

1804
02:27:31.634 --> 02:27:33.594
Media is nothing
but neuro-trigger response

1805
02:27:33.677 --> 02:27:34.887
and viral conditioning.

1806
02:27:34.970 --> 02:27:36.472
Wait, what are you two
talking about?

1807
02:27:38.724 --> 02:27:40.559
Cat videos.

1808
02:27:40.643 --> 02:27:44.396
What we need is
a series of videos

1809
02:27:44.480 --> 02:27:46.815
that we call "The Catrix."
